{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570194700,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4b80ccf001V7lW9oL6yRBRGM","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4b8042f001qFC6jbH33x6TWE","type":"tool","id":"call_40029578c3b6481bb20413f3","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/iterations/iteration-001.md, lines 1-100\n1: # Review Iteration 1 — correctness\n2: \n3: ## Dispatcher\n4: \n5: - Mode: review; target agent `@deep-review`; detached fan-out lineage `doctor-install`.\n6: - Session: `fanout-doctor-install-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1, lineageMode new.\n7: - Artifact root: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install`.\n8: - Dimension: correctness. Budget profile: verify.\n9: - Operator review focus: device behaviour across claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh; safety of a mutating offer; holdout hygiene; docs that disagree with code. This iteration addressed the first two where the doctor-install engines encode them: the per-runtime diagnostic tables, and the mutate path of `agents-md-embed.cjs` (backup, digest, rollback). Holdout hygiene and doc/code disagreement are scheduled for iterations 3 and 4; no holdout file was opened here.\n10: \n11: ## Files Reviewed\n12: \n13: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:39-149`\n14: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:40-206`\n15: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:628-743` (A10 runtime copies), `:597-626` (A9), `:216-261` (A1)\n16: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:91-102` (allowlist/folded copies), `:642-872` (composition), `:1243-1415` (plan/apply), `:1429-1524` (restore)\n17: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json` (`runtime_copies` block)\n18: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs:460-503` (A10 pointer expectations)\n19: - Context evidence: `.codex/hooks.json`, `.claude/settings.json`, `.cursor/hooks.json`, `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, `.opencode/hooks/skill-advisor/*` (runtime surfaces, read-only)\n20: \n21: ## Findings - New\n22: \n23: ### P0 Findings\n24: \n25: None.\n26: \n27: ### P1 Findings\n28: \n29: 1. **A failed write mid-apply leaves a half-embedded tree and prints no undo** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1364` -- `commandApply` writes every target in a bare `for` loop after `writeBackup`, and only reaches the rollback at `:1392-1401` once every write has returned. A throw from `fs.writeFileSync`/`fs.rmSync` (EACCES, EROFS, ENOSPC) propagates through `main`'s non-`UsageError`/`PreconditionError` path, so already-written targets stay written, the post-write preservation proof never runs, and the `backup:`/`undo:` lines at `:1407-1408` are never printed.\n30:    - Case: `AGENTS.md` is replaced and `CLAUDE.md` receives its pointer, then `.cursor/rules/repo-local.md` fails to write because `.cursor` is mounted read-only; the command exits 2 with an uncaught error and the operator never learns the backup directory that holds the pre-run bytes.\n31:    - Finding class: class-of-bug\n32:    - Scope proof: the only rollback is `restoreFromBackup` at `:1397`, reached exclusively from the `after.dropped.length > 0` branch at `:1395`; `rg -n \"restoreFromBackup\" agents-md-embed.cjs` shows no other caller, and no `try`/`catch` wraps the write loop `:1364-1374`.\n33:    - Affected surface hints: [\"commandApply write loop\", \"restoreFromBackup\", \"undo output\"]\n34:    - Claim adjudication:\n35:      ```json\n36:      {\"type\":\"correctness\",\"claim\":\"A write failure after the first target leaves earlier targets mutated and never prints the undo command, so the operator cannot recover from the run's own output.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1364\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1395\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1407\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"searched for a try/catch or rollback around the write loop and for a caller that restores on non-zero exit; found none\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"the backup directory is discoverable by digest and the operator could run restore by hand, so the harm is recoverability rather than permanent loss\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"confidence\":0.7,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"downgrade to P2 if docs state that a failed apply is expected to be recovered by locating the backup directory by hand\"}\n37:      ```\n38: \n39: ### P2 Findings\n40: \n41: 2. **A symlinked `.codex/AGENTS.md` reports PASS while the manifest declares that path absent** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:709` -- `copyVerdict` returns `PASS / symlink` whenever the link's basename is the root file, before `expectsAbsent` (`:677`) is consulted. `expectsAbsent` is only read in the `!exists` branch (`:704-706`), so the manifest row `{\"path\":\".codex/AGENTS.md\",\"expect\":[\"absent\"],\"why\":\"Codex loads the root document as project instructions, so a second copy under its own directory is a copy nothing reads\"}` is never enforced for a link.\n42:    - Case: a migration leaves `.codex/AGENTS.md -> ../AGENTS.md`; A10 reports `7/7 copies as expected` and exit 0, so an operator is told Codex is clean while the duplicate surface the manifest calls unread still exists.\n43:    - Finding class: instance-only\n44:    - Scope proof: the symlink branch `:709-713` precedes every `expect` read; `rg -n \"expectsAbsent\"` shows its two uses at `:677` and `:704` only.\n45:    - Affected surface hints: [\"A10 runtime copies\", \"runtime_copies manifest expectations\"]\n46: 3. **The CLAUDE.md pointer verdict claims every line names AGENTS.md while only one line must** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:731` -- the pass detail at `:732` reads `every line names ${root_file}`, but `namesRoot` is built with `.some(...)` at `:727`. A file with one `@AGENTS.md` line plus arbitrary local instructions passes as a pointer, and the report says all of its lines name the root document.\n47:    - Case: `CLAUDE.md` containing `@AGENTS.md` and `Always answer in Dutch` is reported as `pointer - every line names AGENTS.md`, so the operator reads a claim the check never tested.\n48:    - Finding class: instance-only\n49:    - Scope proof: `namesRoot` is used once, at `:731`; the detail string at `:732` is the only place the universal claim is printed.\n50:    - Affected surface hints: [\"A10 runtime copies\", \"CLAUDE.md pointer verdict\"]\n51: 4. **The preservation proof's fourth claim is computed and never enforced** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:598` -- `preservationCheck` returns `foreign` (lines outside the block that the template does not ship), but `commandPlan` (`:1251-1268`) and `commandApply` (`:1392-1401`) branch only on `dropped`. The JSDoc at `:499-512` presents four claims; the fourth can be non-empty while the run still reports `STATUS=OK`.\n52:    - Case: any future composition change that emits a line outside the block (for example writing a router pointer above the template) is reported as `foreign` to a caller that never reads it, so the plan and apply both pass a tree whose outside-block text is not template text.\n53:    - Finding class: instance-only\n54:    - Scope proof: `rg -n \"foreign\"` in the engine shows construction at `:587-596` and the return at `:598`, with no consumer in `commandPlan` or `commandApply`.\n55:    - Affected surface hints: [\"preservationCheck\", \"commandPlan\", \"commandApply\"]\n56: \n57: ## Traceability Checks\n58: \n59: | Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\n60: |----------|-------|--------|-------|\n61: | spec_code | core | partial | The doctor-install contract test (`doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:80-120`) declares the install route read-only; this iteration read code only, packet docs follow in iteration 3. |\n62: | checklist_evidence | core | pending | No checklist row was claimed as verified in this iteration. |\n63: | skill_agent | overlay | notApplicable | No skill or agent definition is in this lineage's scope. |\n64: | agent_cross_runtime | overlay | partial | Runtime coverage checked against `.codex/hooks.json`, `.claude/settings.json`, `.cursor/hooks.json`, `.devin/hooks.v1.json` and `.opencode/hooks/skill-advisor/`. |\n65: | feature_catalog_code | overlay | pending | Scheduled for iteration 3. |\n66: | playbook_capability | overlay | pending | Scheduled for iteration 3. |\n67: \n68: ## Integration Evidence\n69: \n70: No command, workflow, skill or MCP surface was executed in this iteration. The only integration claims are structural: A10's runtime table is compared against the repository's own runtime hook directories, and `hook-wiring-check.cjs`'s four-runtime table is compared against `.opencode/hooks/skill-advisor/{claude,codex,cursor,devin}`, which is the exact set of runtimes that carry an advisor hook entry here.\n71: \n72: ## Edge Cases\n73: \n74: - The review scope lists 28 `doctor-install` paths; `agents-md-embed.cjs` imports `./lib/agents-md-sections.cjs` and `./release-update.cjs`, which are outside the scope list. They were read as context only, and no finding depends on their behavior.\n75: - `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` reads `.skilled/commands/doctor/install.md`, which is not in the scope list. Treated as unchanged context; no coverage claim is made for it.\n76: - All seven runtime directories exist in this checkout, so the per-runtime conclusions rest on the repository's surfaces, not only on the changed files. A consumer checkout may have fewer runtime folders, which is why `hook-wiring-check` skips an absent runtime folder by design.\n77: \n78: ## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n79: \n80: - `hook-wiring-check.cjs:39-68` names exactly the four runtimes that carry an advisor hook entry in this repository; `.opencode`, `.pi` and `.dsh` carry no `user-prompt-submit` advisor entry, so their absence from the table is not a false clean.\n81: - `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:108` reads the nested `hooks.UserPromptSubmit` shape, which matches the checked-in `.codex/hooks.json` shape; `hook-wiring-check.cjs:105-112` also accepts the top-level shape, so the two checks do not disagree on this repository.\n82: - `agents-md-embed.cjs:888-906` (`assertWritable`) checks containment before allowlist membership and resolves links, matching the mutation boundary the YAML declares.\n83: - `agents-md-check.cjs:627-651` prints an unmeasured copy as a line, so an UNKNOWN row cannot read as a checked pass.\n84: \n85: ## Ruled Out\n86: \n87: - **Codex approval check parses only the nested hook shape** — ruled out: `.codex/hooks.json` wraps its events in `hooks`, and `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:108` reads that shape; the broader top-level acceptance in `hook-wiring-check.cjs` is a superset, not a disagreement.\n88: - **Hook wiring omits opencode/pi/dsh** — ruled out: `.opencode/hooks/skill-advisor/` contains adapter directories for claude, codex, cursor and devin only, so the four-runtime table matches the advisor hook's actual reach in this repository.\n89: - **`expect: [\"absent\"]` is dead for `.codex/AGENTS.md` in every state** — narrowed, not ruled out: a regular identical copy is still a FINDING at `:720-722`; only the symlink branch bypasses the expectation.\n90: \n91: ## Next Focus\n92: \n93: - Dimension: correctness\n94: - Focus area: `doctor-install.yaml`, `doctor-setup.yaml`, `doctor-setup-presentation.txt`, `doctor-install-presentation.txt`, and the `_routes.yaml` rows that surface them\n95: - Reason: iteration 1 covered the scripts; the mutation safety of the install/setup offers lives in the YAML step ordering and the presentation wording\n96: - Rotation status: first pass on the YAML assets\n97: - Blocked/productive carry-forward: symlink/expectation and proof-consumer findings stay open for a later confirmation pass, not a retry of the same read\n98: - Required evidence: direct read of each step's mutation boundary plus the route row that offers it\n99: \n100: Review verdict: CONDITIONAL","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/iterations/iteration-001.md, lines 1-100\n1: # Review Iteration 1 — correctness\n2: \n3: ## Dispatcher\n4: \n5: - Mode: review; target agent `@deep-review`; detached fan-out lineage `doctor-install`.\n6: - Session: `fanout-doctor-install-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1, lineageMode new.\n7: - Artifact root: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install`.\n8: - Dimension: correctness. Budget profile: verify.\n9: - Operator review focus: device behaviour across claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh; safety of a mutating offer; holdout hygiene; docs that disagree with code. This iteration addressed the first two where the doctor-install engines encode them: the per-runtime diagnostic tables, and the mutate path of `agents-md-embed.cjs` (backup, digest, rollback). Holdout hygiene and doc/code disagreement are scheduled for iterations 3 and 4; no holdout file was opened here.\n10: \n11: ## Files Reviewed\n12: \n13: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:39-149`\n14: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:40-206`\n15: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:628-743` (A10 runtime copies), `:597-626` (A9), `:216-261` (A1)\n16: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:91-102` (allowlist/folded copies), `:642-872` (composition), `:1243-1415` (plan/apply), `:1429-1524` (restore)\n17: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json` (`runtime_copies` block)\n18: - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs:460-503` (A10 pointer expectations)\n19: - Context evidence: `.codex/hooks.json`, `.claude/settings.json`, `.cursor/hooks.json`, `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, `.opencode/hooks/skill-advisor/*` (runtime surfaces, read-only)\n20: \n21: ## Findings - New\n22: \n23: ### P0 Findings\n24: \n25: None.\n26: \n27: ### P1 Findings\n28: \n29: 1. **A failed write mid-apply leaves a half-embedded tree and prints no undo** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1364` -- `commandApply` writes every target in a bare `for` loop after `writeBackup`, and only reaches the rollback at `:1392-1401` once every write has returned. A throw from `fs.writeFileSync`/`fs.rmSync` (EACCES, EROFS, ENOSPC) propagates through `main`'s non-`UsageError`/`PreconditionError` path, so already-written targets stay written, the post-write preservation proof never runs, and the `backup:`/`undo:` lines at `:1407-1408` are never printed.\n30:    - Case: `AGENTS.md` is replaced and `CLAUDE.md` receives its pointer, then `.cursor/rules/repo-local.md` fails to write because `.cursor` is mounted read-only; the command exits 2 with an uncaught error and the operator never learns the backup directory that holds the pre-run bytes.\n31:    - Finding class: class-of-bug\n32:    - Scope proof: the only rollback is `restoreFromBackup` at `:1397`, reached exclusively from the `after.dropped.length > 0` branch at `:1395`; `rg -n \"restoreFromBackup\" agents-md-embed.cjs` shows no other caller, and no `try`/`catch` wraps the write loop `:1364-1374`.\n33:    - Affected surface hints: [\"commandApply write loop\", \"restoreFromBackup\", \"undo output\"]\n34:    - Claim adjudication:\n35:      ```json\n36:      {\"type\":\"correctness\",\"claim\":\"A write failure after the first target leaves earlier targets mutated and never prints the undo command, so the operator cannot recover from the run's own output.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1364\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1395\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1407\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"searched for a try/catch or rollback around the write loop and for a caller that restores on non-zero exit; found none\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"the backup directory is discoverable by digest and the operator could run restore by hand, so the harm is recoverability rather than permanent loss\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"confidence\":0.7,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"downgrade to P2 if docs state that a failed apply is expected to be recovered by locating the backup directory by hand\"}\n37:      ```\n38: \n39: ### P2 Findings\n40: \n41: 2. **A symlinked `.codex/AGENTS.md` reports PASS while the manifest declares that path absent** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:709` -- `copyVerdict` returns `PASS / symlink` whenever the link's basename is the root file, before `expectsAbsent` (`:677`) is consulted. `expectsAbsent` is only read in the `!exists` branch (`:704-706`), so the manifest row `{\"path\":\".codex/AGENTS.md\",\"expect\":[\"absent\"],\"why\":\"Codex loads the root document as project instructions, so a second copy under its own directory is a copy nothing reads\"}` is never enforced for a link.\n42:    - Case: a migration leaves `.codex/AGENTS.md -> ../AGENTS.md`; A10 reports `7/7 copies as expected` and exit 0, so an operator is told Codex is clean while the duplicate surface the manifest calls unread still exists.\n43:    - Finding class: instance-only\n44:    - Scope proof: the symlink branch `:709-713` precedes every `expect` read; `rg -n \"expectsAbsent\"` shows its two uses at `:677` and `:704` only.\n45:    - Affected surface hints: [\"A10 runtime copies\", \"runtime_copies manifest expectations\"]\n46: 3. **The CLAUDE.md pointer verdict claims every line names AGENTS.md while only one line must** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:731` -- the pass detail at `:732` reads `every line names ${root_file}`, but `namesRoot` is built with `.some(...)` at `:727`. A file with one `@AGENTS.md` line plus arbitrary local instructions passes as a pointer, and the report says all of its lines name the root document.\n47:    - Case: `CLAUDE.md` containing `@AGENTS.md` and `Always answer in Dutch` is reported as `pointer - every line names AGENTS.md`, so the operator reads a claim the check never tested.\n48:    - Finding class: instance-only\n49:    - Scope proof: `namesRoot` is used once, at `:731`; the detail string at `:732` is the only place the universal claim is printed.\n50:    - Affected surface hints: [\"A10 runtime copies\", \"CLAUDE.md pointer verdict\"]\n51: 4. **The preservation proof's fourth claim is computed and never enforced** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:598` -- `preservationCheck` returns `foreign` (lines outside the block that the template does not ship), but `commandPlan` (`:1251-1268`) and `commandApply` (`:1392-1401`) branch only on `dropped`. The JSDoc at `:499-512` presents four claims; the fourth can be non-empty while the run still reports `STATUS=OK`.\n52:    - Case: any future composition change that emits a line outside the block (for example writing a router pointer above the template) is reported as `foreign` to a caller that never reads it, so the plan and apply both pass a tree whose outside-block text is not template text.\n53:    - Finding class: instance-only\n54:    - Scope proof: `rg -n \"foreign\"` in the engine shows construction at `:587-596` and the return at `:598`, with no consumer in `commandPlan` or `commandApply`.\n55:    - Affected surface hints: [\"preservationCheck\", \"commandPlan\", \"commandApply\"]\n56: \n57: ## Traceability Checks\n58: \n59: | Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\n60: |----------|-------|--------|-------|\n61: | spec_code | core | partial | The doctor-install contract test (`doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:80-120`) declares the install route read-only; this iteration read code only, packet docs follow in iteration 3. |\n62: | checklist_evidence | core | pending | No checklist row was claimed as verified in this iteration. |\n63: | skill_agent | overlay | notApplicable | No skill or agent definition is in this lineage's scope. |\n64: | agent_cross_runtime | overlay | partial | Runtime coverage checked against `.codex/hooks.json`, `.claude/settings.json`, `.cursor/hooks.json`, `.devin/hooks.v1.json` and `.opencode/hooks/skill-advisor/`. |\n65: | feature_catalog_code | overlay | pending | Scheduled for iteration 3. |\n66: | playbook_capability | overlay | pending | Scheduled for iteration 3. |\n67: \n68: ## Integration Evidence\n69: \n70: No command, workflow, skill or MCP surface was executed in this iteration. The only integration claims are structural: A10's runtime table is compared against the repository's own runtime hook directories, and `hook-wiring-check.cjs`'s four-runtime table is compared against `.opencode/hooks/skill-advisor/{claude,codex,cursor,devin}`, which is the exact set of runtimes that carry an advisor hook entry here.\n71: \n72: ## Edge Cases\n73: \n74: - The review scope lists 28 `doctor-install` paths; `agents-md-embed.cjs` imports `./lib/agents-md-sections.cjs` and `./release-update.cjs`, which are outside the scope list. They were read as context only, and no finding depends on their behavior.\n75: - `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` reads `.skilled/commands/doctor/install.md`, which is not in the scope list. Treated as unchanged context; no coverage claim is made for it.\n76: - All seven runtime directories exist in this checkout, so the per-runtime conclusions rest on the repository's surfaces, not only on the changed files. A consumer checkout may have fewer runtime folders, which is why `hook-wiring-check` skips an absent runtime folder by design.\n77: \n78: ## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n79: \n80: - `hook-wiring-check.cjs:39-68` names exactly the four runtimes that carry an advisor hook entry in this repository; `.opencode`, `.pi` and `.dsh` carry no `user-prompt-submit` advisor entry, so their absence from the table is not a false clean.\n81: - `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:108` reads the nested `hooks.UserPromptSubmit` shape, which matches the checked-in `.codex/hooks.json` shape; `hook-wiring-check.cjs:105-112` also accepts the top-level shape, so the two checks do not disagree on this repository.\n82: - `agents-md-embed.cjs:888-906` (`assertWritable`) checks containment before allowlist membership and resolves links, matching the mutation boundary the YAML declares.\n83: - `agents-md-check.cjs:627-651` prints an unmeasured copy as a line, so an UNKNOWN row cannot read as a checked pass.\n84: \n85: ## Ruled Out\n86: \n87: - **Codex approval check parses only the nested hook shape** — ruled out: `.codex/hooks.json` wraps its events in `hooks`, and `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:108` reads that shape; the broader top-level acceptance in `hook-wiring-check.cjs` is a superset, not a disagreement.\n88: - **Hook wiring omits opencode/pi/dsh** — ruled out: `.opencode/hooks/skill-advisor/` contains adapter directories for claude, codex, cursor and devin only, so the four-runtime table matches the advisor hook's actual reach in this repository.\n89: - **`expect: [\"absent\"]` is dead for `.codex/AGENTS.md` in every state** — narrowed, not ruled out: a regular identical copy is still a FINDING at `:720-722`; only the symlink branch bypasses the expectation.\n90: \n91: ## Next Focus\n92: \n93: - Dimension: correctness\n94: - Focus area: `doctor-install.yaml`, `doctor-setup.yaml`, `doctor-setup-presentation.txt`, `doctor-install-presentation.txt`, and the `_routes.yaml` rows that surface them\n95: - Reason: iteration 1 covered the scripts; the mutation safety of the install/setup offers lives in the YAML step ordering and the presentation wording\n96: - Rotation status: first pass on the YAML assets\n97: - Blocked/productive carry-forward: symlink/expectation and proof-consumer findings stay open for a later confirmation pass, not a retry of the same read\n98: - Required evidence: direct read of each step's mutation boundary plus the route row that offers it\n99: \n100: Review verdict: CONDITIONAL"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570194127,"end":1794570194700}}}}
