{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570334157,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4ba2cf9001bGmGJm5n8DLTsC","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4ba0913001nbCGuPg1t4fiFk","type":"tool","id":"call_34e3e3c79b97445099250a9b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git diff 320e7b64d4..HEAD -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\nindex 257b64487b..9fcd4decdc 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\n@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ Render one row per leg, in the workflow's order.\n | runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n | advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n | embedder | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` |\n-| delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session |\n+| delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session. Absent Codex advisor entry: the repair line the check prints |\n \n ## 4. Result Templates\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\nindex 23d5e54930..c271c23808 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\n@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ mutation_boundaries:\n   allowed_targets: []\n   forbidden_targets:\n     - \"**/*\"\n-  invariant: \"Every leg runs in its check-only form. This route MUST NOT regenerate the trigger index, sync a runtime mirror, start the advisor daemon, install hooks or provision the tree. A failing leg prints the doctor command that repairs it; repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of this diagnostic.\"\n+  invariant: \"Every leg runs in its check-only form. This route MUST NOT regenerate the trigger index, sync a runtime mirror, start the advisor daemon, install hooks or provision the tree. A failing leg prints the doctor command that repairs it; repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of this diagnostic. The one write outside the repository is the advisor CLI creating its socket directory, /tmp/system-skill-advisor unless SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR names another, when that directory is absent. No leg makes it on purpose.\"\n \n # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n@@ -56,9 +56,9 @@ execution:\n     - \"Leg sk-git: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs --tool=<name>, where <name> is the AI tool executing this command: claude, codex, devin, cursor, opencode, pi or dsh. On any other runtime, run it without --tool, because the battery accepts no other name. Exit 0 passes. Exit 3 is DEGRADED, not a failure: no check failed, but one is UNKNOWN or DEGRADED, so the row names /doctor:git setup to show which. Exit 2 is a usage error or a crash and is ERROR. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:git setup.\"\n     - \"Leg trigger-index: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs --check --json. Exit 0 passes. Exit 1 (stale documents) or 2 and higher (unreadable index) fails, with repair /doctor:speckit.\"\n     - \"Leg runtime-mirrors: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check. Exit 0 passes. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors.\"\n-    - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.\"\n+    - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts, fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent>, degraded <rollingDegradedRate as a percent> and last record <lastRecordAt> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status. When data.hookHealth is absent, show hook health not recorded under the leg, because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet: OpenCode has no prompt hook that writes one and an unapproved Codex hook never runs. It never changes the leg's status.\"\n     - \"Leg embedder: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --timeout-ms 1500 --warm-only. Exit 75 is SKIP, as for the advisor leg, because the daemon is not running. Exit 0 with data.semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled true and data.semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage.embedded above 0 is PASS. Any other result is DEGRADED, never FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor embedder.\"\n-    - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n+    - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n     - \"Last session hop (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs history --last 1 and show its first output line under the result as the last session hop, plus its open notes line when it prints one. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n     - \"Claude context window (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs window and show its line. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n     - \"Orphan processes (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/orphan-process-check.cjs --summary and show its line. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml\nindex 6963263e88..f8bcaa2bf5 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml\n@@ -122,8 +122,9 @@ workflow:\n     runs_when: \"phase_3_approval approved\"\n     activities:\n       - \"When the install step is missing, print the Ollama install command the install guide prints and stop with STATUS=FAIL, naming that command as the next step. Never install or upgrade Ollama from this route.\"\n-      - \"When the start step is missing, run `ollama serve` in the background with a readable log, record the pid this run started and poll `/api/version` until it answers or a short deadline passes. A server that never answers is STATUS=FAIL naming the start and the log path, and the pull and scan steps do not run.\"\n-      - \"When the pull step is missing, run `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` only once the server answers. A non-zero exit is STATUS=FAIL naming the pull, and the scan step does not run.\"\n+      - \"When the resolved URL's host is not 127.0.0.1, localhost or ::1, start and pull nothing. That server is the operator's, so end with STATUS=FAIL naming the URL and the install guide's start and pull commands.\"\n+      - \"When the start step is missing, run `OLLAMA_HOST=<host:port of the resolved URL> ollama serve` in the background with a readable log, record the pid this run started and poll `/api/version` until it answers or a short deadline passes. A server that never answers is STATUS=FAIL naming the start and the log path, and the pull and scan steps do not run.\"\n+      - \"When the pull step is missing, run `OLLAMA_HOST=<host:port of the resolved URL> ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` only once the server answers. A non-zero exit is STATUS=FAIL naming the pull, and the scan step does not run.\"\n       - \"Never pull a model the plan did not list, never remove a model and never restart a server this run did not start.\"\n \n   phase_5_scan:\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml\nindex 264f9c8ed8..019a00069f 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml\n@@ -66,4 +66,7 @@ execution:\n output: |\n   STATUS=OK when the engine exits 0. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n   STATUS=WARN when the engine exits 1. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n+  STATUS=WARN when the engine exits 0 and the hook-wiring check exits 1. Show each hook-missing line and the repair the step names.\n   STATUS=FAIL when the engine exits 2 or cannot run. Name the accepted invocation (/doctor:symlink check --root <dir> [flags]) and quote the engine message.\n+  STATUS=FAIL when the hook-wiring check exits 2. Quote its message.\n+  When the engine and the hook-wiring check end on different statuses, the worse one wins: FAIL over WARN over OK.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md b/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\nindex 17b68fd61e..ed94742885 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\n@@ -79,3 +79,4 @@ It reports DEGRADED when exit 0 has any other freshness value and names `/doctor\n It reports FAIL when exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON and names `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`.\n It reports SKIP when exit 75 lacks that field because the daemon is stopped.\n It reports FAIL for any other exit with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n+When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded and names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, the setting that turns the records on.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\nindex 257b64487b..9fcd4decdc 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\n@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ Render one row per leg, in the workflow's order.\n | runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n | advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n | embedder | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` |\n-| delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session |\n+| delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session. Absent Codex advisor entry: the repair line the check prints |\n \n ## 4. Result Templates\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\nindex 23d5e54930..c271c23808 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\n@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ mutation_boundaries:\n   allowed_targets: []\n   forbidden_targets:\n     - \"**/*\"\n-  invariant: \"Every leg runs in its check-only form. This route MUST NOT regenerate the trigger index, sync a runtime mirror, start the advisor daemon, install hooks or provision the tree. A failing leg prints the doctor command that repairs it; repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of this diagnostic.\"\n+  invariant: \"Every leg runs in its check-only form. This route MUST NOT regenerate the trigger index, sync a runtime mirror, start the advisor daemon, install hooks or provision the tree. A failing leg prints the doctor command that repairs it; repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of this diagnostic. The one write outside the repository is the advisor CLI creating its socket directory, /tmp/system-skill-advisor unless SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR names another, when that directory is absent. No leg makes it on purpose.\"\n \n # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n@@ -56,9 +56,9 @@ execution:\n     - \"Leg sk-git: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs --tool=<name>, where <name> is the AI tool executing this command: claude, codex, devin, cursor, opencode, pi or dsh. On any other runtime, run it without --tool, because the battery accepts no other name. Exit 0 passes. Exit 3 is DEGRADED, not a failure: no check failed, but one is UNKNOWN or DEGRADED, so the row names /doctor:git setup to show which. Exit 2 is a usage error or a crash and is ERROR. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:git setup.\"\n     - \"Leg trigger-index: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs --check --json. Exit 0 passes. Exit 1 (stale documents) or 2 and higher (unreadable index) fails, with repair /doctor:speckit.\"\n     - \"Leg runtime-mirrors: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check. Exit 0 passes. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors.\"\n-    - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.\"\n+    - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts, fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent>, degraded <rollingDegradedRate as a percent> and last record <lastRecordAt> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status. When data.hookHealth is absent, show hook health not recorded under the leg, because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet: OpenCode has no prompt hook that writes one and an unapproved Codex hook never runs. It never changes the leg's status.\"\n     - \"Leg embedder: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --timeout-ms 1500 --warm-only. Exit 75 is SKIP, as for the advisor leg, because the daemon is not running. Exit 0 with data.semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled true and data.semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage.embedded above 0 is PASS. Any other result is DEGRADED, never FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor embedder.\"\n-    - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n+    - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n     - \"Last session hop (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs history --last 1 and show its first output line under the result as the last session hop, plus its open notes line when it prints one. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n     - \"Claude context window (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs window and show its line. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n     - \"Orphan processes (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/orphan-process-check.cjs --summary and show its line. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml\nindex 6963263e88..f8bcaa2bf5 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml\n@@ -122,8 +122,9 @@ workflow:\n     runs_when: \"phase_3_approval approved\"\n     activities:\n       - \"When the install step is missing, print the Ollama install command the install guide prints and stop with STATUS=FAIL, naming that command as the next step. Never install or upgrade Ollama from this route.\"\n-      - \"When the start step is missing, run `ollama serve` in the background with a readable log, record the pid this run started and poll `/api/version` until it answers or a short deadline passes. A server that never answers is STATUS=FAIL naming the start and the log path, and the pull and scan steps do not run.\"\n-      - \"When the pull step is missing, run `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` only once the server answers. A non-zero exit is STATUS=FAIL naming the pull, and the scan step does not run.\"\n+      - \"When the resolved URL's host is not 127.0.0.1, localhost or ::1, start and pull nothing. That server is the operator's, so end with STATUS=FAIL naming the URL and the install guide's start and pull commands.\"\n+      - \"When the start step is missing, run `OLLAMA_HOST=<host:port of the resolved URL> ollama serve` in the background with a readable log, record the pid this run started and poll `/api/version` until it answers or a short deadline passes. A server that never answers is STATUS=FAIL naming the start and the log path, and the pull and scan steps do not run.\"\n+      - \"When the pull step is missing, run `OLLAMA_HOST=<host:port of the resolved URL> ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` only once the server answers. A non-zero exit is STATUS=FAIL naming the pull, and the scan step does not run.\"\n       - \"Never pull a model the plan did not list, never remove a model and never restart a server this run did not start.\"\n \n   phase_5_scan:\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml\nindex 264f9c8ed8..019a00069f 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml\n@@ -66,4 +66,7 @@ execution:\n output: |\n   STATUS=OK when the engine exits 0. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n   STATUS=WARN when the engine exits 1. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n+  STATUS=WARN when the engine exits 0 and the hook-wiring check exits 1. Show each hook-missing line and the repair the step names.\n   STATUS=FAIL when the engine exits 2 or cannot run. Name the accepted invocation (/doctor:symlink check --root <dir> [flags]) and quote the engine message.\n+  STATUS=FAIL when the hook-wiring check exits 2. Quote its message.\n+  When the engine and the hook-wiring check end on different statuses, the worse one wins: FAIL over WARN over OK.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md b/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\nindex 17b68fd61e..ed94742885 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\n@@ -79,3 +79,4 @@ It reports DEGRADED when exit 0 has any other freshness value and names `/doctor\n It reports FAIL when exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON and names `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`.\n It reports SKIP when exit 75 lacks that field because the daemon is stopped.\n It reports FAIL for any other exit with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n+When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded and names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, the setting that turns the records on.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git diff 320e7b64d4..HEAD -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570333433,"end":1794570334157}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570334167,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4ba2b32002cRCSKYEP0rcTZe","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4ba0913001nbCGuPg1t4fiFk","type":"tool","id":"call_49075b7df9c3413f8eb4eb0b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git diff 320e7b64d4..HEAD -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\nindex d53dde5c4a..6fe597d842 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n@@ -84,7 +84,7 @@ workflow:\n       - \"Exit 0 with NOTHING TO DO means the repository is already in its target state, which the engine prints without a plan. Render the presentation contract's unchanged result with the engine's own notes, ask nothing, write nothing and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK.\"\n       - \"A finding line that says the composed document is past the byte ceiling is a finding rather than a refusal: every carried line is kept, because preservation outranks the budget. Show it with the plan and let the operator decide. A run whose composition drops a line refuses instead, exits 1 and writes nothing; print the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL and stop.\"\n       - \"If dry_run is true, render the presentation contract's dry-run result from the plan's own lines, print the dry-run line and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK. A dry run asks nothing and writes nothing, so it runs no question and no apply.\"\n-      - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing manifest, a symlinked root document or one of the two markers present without the other. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:agents-md embed), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n+      - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing manifest, a symlinked root document, a symlinked REPO RULES.md or Cursor mirror the run would write, or one of the two markers present without the other. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:agents-md embed), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n \n   phase_3_approval:\n     purpose: \"Ask the one embed question against the plan on screen, and write only after its yes\"\n@@ -100,7 +100,8 @@ workflow:\n       - \"Exit 2 with a message that the plan digest does not match the composition now means the tree changed after the plan, so nothing was written. Quote the engine's message, offer the plan again against the current tree, and end with STATUS=FAIL. Never retry the apply with a recomposed digest of your own: the point of the digest is that the approved bytes are the written bytes.\"\n       - \"Exit 0 means the write ran. Keep exactly the lines the engine printed: its apply line, one wrote or removed line per path, the pointer-sync line, the repo-rules line after a router write, the preservation line, the check-after line, the backup line, the undo line, one copy line per overwritten file and STATUS=OK.\"\n       - \"A nonzero pointer-sync line is the one verdict the run leaves unresolved: the generator rewrites an existing .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md and never creates a missing one, so a repository without that file ends with exit 1 and the mirror still missing. Keep the line as printed, render it in the result's Pointer sync: field, never list .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md in Files changed on the strength of the allowlist that names it, and render a Next: line naming /doctor:runtime-mirrors, whose rows list each generated mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker. The repair chain for the pointer file itself is the presentation's troubleshooting row for A10, because that route does not check it. A repo-rules line that reports an error belongs in Router: the same way.\"\n-      - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line. The engine restored from the backup by itself and kept the backup. Quote the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n+      - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line or a `foreign:` line. The engine restored from the backup by itself unless it printed `nothing was restored`, and kept the backup. Quote the lines the proof named, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it when the restore ran. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n+      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step.\"\n       - \"An allowlist refusal exits 2 before a backup exists, because every path the run would touch is resolved before the first byte. Quote the message and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n \n   phase_5_reread:\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\nindex b736a2e477..b08fe38e6e 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n@@ -253,7 +253,7 @@ Next: [the repair, or the accepted invocation]\n STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[code]\"\n ```\n \n-A check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"`. An embed that exits 1 after its proof found a dropped line restored from the backup by itself, so its `Changed:` is `none` and its `Next:` names the file whose line went missing.\n+A check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"`. An embed that exits 1 after its proof found a dropped line restored from the backup by itself, so its `Changed:` is `none` and its `Next:` names the file whose line went missing. An embed that exits 3 had a write fail after its backup. Its Changed: is none when the output holds restored:, and otherwise the reply says the tree is partly written and its Next: is the undo command the engine printed.\n \n ## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\nindex 0d6e07592e..bbc8c02f91 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\n@@ -75,7 +75,9 @@ The example carries all four answers so the shape of a full reply is visible. Ne\n | `embed` | step 2 stays | The repo keeps its own `AGENTS.md` and the shipped sections are refreshed into it |\n | `link` | step 1 gains `--link-instructions`, step 2 is dropped | `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` become links into the checkout |\n \n-A runtime name outside the seven, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n+A runtime name outside claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin and pi or the ones already there, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n+\n+DSH is not offered, because the link manifest has no DSH row.\n \n ## 5. The Symlink Check\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml\nindex 10edf61376..8910d8f702 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml\n@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ upstream_assets:\n inputs:\n   target: \"The command takes no positional target. A whole argument of list, ? or menu prints the ordered install steps and stops.\"\n   root: \"The target repository's absolute path, supplied with --root or in the consolidated prompt.\"\n-  runtimes: \"The runtime list, supplied with --runtimes or in the consolidated prompt; the operator can choose the runtimes already there.\"\n+  runtimes: \"The runtime list, supplied with --runtimes or in the consolidated prompt; the operator can choose the runtimes already there. DSH is not offered, because the link manifest has no dsh row.\"\n   link_shape: \"The operator's choice of auto, whole or merge; auto is recommended.\"\n   instruction_choice: \"The operator's choice of embed or link; embed is recommended and keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md.\"\n   json_output: \"True when --json is passed; print one JSON object and nothing else.\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\nindex d53dde5c4a..6fe597d842 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n@@ -84,7 +84,7 @@ workflow:\n       - \"Exit 0 with NOTHING TO DO means the repository is already in its target state, which the engine prints without a plan. Render the presentation contract's unchanged result with the engine's own notes, ask nothing, write nothing and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK.\"\n       - \"A finding line that says the composed document is past the byte ceiling is a finding rather than a refusal: every carried line is kept, because preservation outranks the budget. Show it with the plan and let the operator decide. A run whose composition drops a line refuses instead, exits 1 and writes nothing; print the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL and stop.\"\n       - \"If dry_run is true, render the presentation contract's dry-run result from the plan's own lines, print the dry-run line and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK. A dry run asks nothing and writes nothing, so it runs no question and no apply.\"\n-      - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing manifest, a symlinked root document or one of the two markers present without the other. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:agents-md embed), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n+      - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing manifest, a symlinked root document, a symlinked REPO RULES.md or Cursor mirror the run would write, or one of the two markers present without the other. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:agents-md embed), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n \n   phase_3_approval:\n     purpose: \"Ask the one embed question against the plan on screen, and write only after its yes\"\n@@ -100,7 +100,8 @@ workflow:\n       - \"Exit 2 with a message that the plan digest does not match the composition now means the tree changed after the plan, so nothing was written. Quote the engine's message, offer the plan again against the current tree, and end with STATUS=FAIL. Never retry the apply with a recomposed digest of your own: the point of the digest is that the approved bytes are the written bytes.\"\n       - \"Exit 0 means the write ran. Keep exactly the lines the engine printed: its apply line, one wrote or removed line per path, the pointer-sync line, the repo-rules line after a router write, the preservation line, the check-after line, the backup line, the undo line, one copy line per overwritten file and STATUS=OK.\"\n       - \"A nonzero pointer-sync line is the one verdict the run leaves unresolved: the generator rewrites an existing .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md and never creates a missing one, so a repository without that file ends with exit 1 and the mirror still missing. Keep the line as printed, render it in the result's Pointer sync: field, never list .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md in Files changed on the strength of the allowlist that names it, and render a Next: line naming /doctor:runtime-mirrors, whose rows list each generated mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker. The repair chain for the pointer file itself is the presentation's troubleshooting row for A10, because that route does not check it. A repo-rules line that reports an error belongs in Router: the same way.\"\n-      - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line. The engine restored from the backup by itself and kept the backup. Quote the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n+      - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line or a `foreign:` line. The engine restored from the backup by itself unless it printed `nothing was restored`, and kept the backup. Quote the lines the proof named, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it when the restore ran. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n+      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step.\"\n       - \"An allowlist refusal exits 2 before a backup exists, because every path the run would touch is resolved before the first byte. Quote the message and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n \n   phase_5_reread:\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\nindex b736a2e477..b08fe38e6e 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n@@ -253,7 +253,7 @@ Next: [the repair, or the accepted invocation]\n STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[code]\"\n ```\n \n-A check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"`. An embed that exits 1 after its proof found a dropped line restored from the backup by itself, so its `Changed:` is `none` and its `Next:` names the file whose line went missing.\n+A check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"`. An embed that exits 1 after its proof found a dropped line restored from the backup by itself, so its `Changed:` is `none` and its `Next:` names the file whose line went missing. An embed that exits 3 had a write fail after its backup. Its Changed: is none when the output holds restored:, and otherwise the reply says the tree is partly written and its Next: is the undo command the engine printed.\n \n ## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\nindex 0d6e07592e..bbc8c02f91 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\n@@ -75,7 +75,9 @@ The example carries all four answers so the shape of a full reply is visible. Ne\n | `embed` | step 2 stays | The repo keeps its own `AGENTS.md` and the shipped sections are refreshed into it |\n | `link` | step 1 gains `--link-instructions`, step 2 is dropped | `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` become links into the checkout |\n \n-A runtime name outside the seven, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n+A runtime name outside claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin and pi or the ones already there, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n+\n+DSH is not offered, because the link manifest has no DSH row.\n \n ## 5. The Symlink Check\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml\nindex 10edf61376..8910d8f702 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml\n@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ upstream_assets:\n inputs:\n   target: \"The command takes no positional target. A whole argument of list, ? or menu prints the ordered install steps and stops.\"\n   root: \"The target repository's absolute path, supplied with --root or in the consolidated prompt.\"\n-  runtimes: \"The runtime list, supplied with --runtimes or in the consolidated prompt; the operator can choose the runtimes already there.\"\n+  runtimes: \"The runtime list, supplied with --runtimes or in the consolidated prompt; the operator can choose the runtimes already there. DSH is not offered, because the link manifest has no dsh row.\"\n   link_shape: \"The operator's choice of auto, whole or merge; auto is recommended.\"\n   instruction_choice: \"The operator's choice of embed or link; embed is recommended and keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md.\"\n   json_output: \"True when --json is passed; print one JSON object and nothing else.\"\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git diff 320e7b64d4..HEAD -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570332978,"end":1794570334167}}}}
