{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570428001,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4bb9ae7001QEEoDWPi3NCRYv","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4bb853d001PD2mD7nfQ3oNtD","type":"tool","id":"call_a6c734ee0c2b4ee08592f426","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog -r 2>/dev/null | head -20"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md:150:**Release validation.** `advisor_validate` runs the regression suite and reports threshold semantics (aggregate vs runtime) plus a prompt-safe `telemetry.outcomes.totals` block. Hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks so `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes. Records carry the runtime that served the turn, the bytes delivered (`emittedBytes`) and whether the directives were suppressed (`directivesSuppressed`). Each hook run writes a health record with no prompt, skill label or error text, and `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The bounded trim writes a temp file and renames it over the log so a crash mid-trim keeps the old log.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md:82:When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded and names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, the setting that turns the records on.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md:42:Each record carries `runtime`, taken from `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` when it names a known runtime and `claude` otherwise. Records carry optional `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. The hook writes a health record to the diagnostics sink on every prompt and adds the skill label and the error text there only when `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set. A record whose answer came from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. Raw prompts never appear in diagnostics. Before exiting, the hook waits up to 100 ms for pending diagnostic writes.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md:150:**Release validation.** `advisor_validate` runs the regression suite and reports threshold semantics (aggregate vs runtime) plus a prompt-safe `telemetry.outcomes.totals` block. Hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks so `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes. Records carry the runtime that served the turn, the bytes delivered (`emittedBytes`) and whether the directives were suppressed (`directivesSuppressed`). Each hook run writes a health record with no prompt, skill label or error text, and `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The bounded trim writes a temp file and renames it over the log so a crash mid-trim keeps the old log.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md:82:When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded and names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, the setting that turns the records on.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md:42:Each record carries `runtime`, taken from `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` when it names a known runtime and `claude` otherwise. Records carry optional `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. The hook writes a health record to the diagnostics sink on every prompt and adds the skill label and the error text there only when `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set. A record whose answer came from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. Raw prompts never appear in diagnostics. Before exiting, the hook waits up to 100 ms for pending diagnostic writes.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -rn \\\"SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog -r 2>/dev/null | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570427111,"end":1794570428001}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570439300,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4bb9ae3002Ya1y9z5MpUksA7","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4bb853d001PD2mD7nfQ3oNtD","type":"tool","id":"call_c374df7c863d4ae382dfa827","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor .opencode/plugins | head -20; sed -n '70,90p' .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/runtime/lib/metrics.js:308:export async function persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(workspaceRoot, record) {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js:20:import { createAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord, persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord, serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord, } from '../../runtime/lib/metrics.js';\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js:132:export function emitDiagnostic(record, writeDiagnostic = (line) => process.stderr.write(`${line}\\n`), persistDiagnostic = persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord) {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts:33:  persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts:519:        await persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(root, createAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts:542:      await persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(root, createAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts:572:        await persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(root, createAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts:591:    await persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(root, createAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts:600:    await persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(root, createAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts:451:export async function persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:40:  persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:242:  persistDiagnostic: typeof persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord = persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord,\nIt shows the Claude context window the relaunch nudge measures against, or the two settings that supply one when none is configured.\nIt shows an orphans line from `orphan-process-check.cjs --summary`.\nThat line counts leftover helper processes and model servers whose launcher died.\nThese lines are informational and never change the status.\nIt writes nothing in the repository and never starts the advisor daemon.\nThe only write outside the repository is the advisor CLI creating its socket directory when that directory is absent.\nThe default socket directory is `/tmp/system-skill-advisor`.\nThe advisor leg reports PASS when exit 0 has `data.freshness` set to `live`.\nIt reports DEGRADED when exit 0 has any other freshness value and names `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\nIt reports FAIL when exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON and names `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`.\nIt reports SKIP when exit 75 lacks that field because the daemon is stopped.\nIt reports FAIL for any other exit with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\nWhen the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded and names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, the setting that turns the records on.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled