{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570615489,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4be79a6001vR7Ih5B0O6c8Af","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4be3485001yhnJI44C1v0K3p","type":"tool","id":"call_e7f9b78c521a46aa82f1643a","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '84,125p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml"},"output":"      - \"Exit 0 with NOTHING TO DO means the repository is already in its target state, which the engine prints without a plan. Render the presentation contract's unchanged result with the engine's own notes, ask nothing, write nothing and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK.\"\n      - \"A finding line that says the composed document is past the byte ceiling is a finding rather than a refusal: every carried line is kept, because preservation outranks the budget. Show it with the plan and let the operator decide. A run whose composition drops a line refuses instead, exits 1 and writes nothing; print the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL and stop.\"\n      - \"If dry_run is true, render the presentation contract's dry-run result from the plan's own lines, print the dry-run line and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK. A dry run asks nothing and writes nothing, so it runs no question and no apply.\"\n      - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing manifest, a symlinked root document, a symlinked REPO RULES.md or Cursor mirror the run would write, or one of the two markers present without the other. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:agents-md embed), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n\n  phase_3_approval:\n    purpose: \"Ask the one embed question against the plan on screen, and write only after its yes\"\n    activities:\n      - \"Ask the embed question once, in the presentation contract's wording, naming the files the plan will create, replace or remove, the backup folder, the router rows the plan would add and the plan digest. The operator answers about the plan the operator has just read, which is this run's plan.\"\n      - \"Any answer other than yes is a no: print the cancelled result naming the declined embed, state Changed: none, and end with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled. Nothing is written.\"\n      - \"Never default an answer, never carry an approval from an earlier run, and never accept a digest the operator has not seen. Phase 4 runs only after this phase's yes.\"\n\n  phase_4_write:\n    purpose: \"Write the approved composition and nothing else, only after the embed yes\"\n    activities:\n      - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs apply --plan-digest \\\"{plan_digest}\\\" with exactly the flags the plan ran with: --root \\\"{root}\\\" when it was given, --keep-claude-md or --remove-claude-md as approved, and --create-router when it was approved. Run it only after the embed yes.\"\n      - \"Exit 2 with a message that the plan digest does not match the composition now means the tree changed after the plan, so nothing was written. Quote the engine's message, offer the plan again against the current tree, and end with STATUS=FAIL. Never retry the apply with a recomposed digest of your own: the point of the digest is that the approved bytes are the written bytes.\"\n      - \"Exit 0 means the write ran. Keep exactly the lines the engine printed: its apply line, one wrote or removed line per path, the pointer-sync line, the repo-rules line after a router write, the preservation line, the check-after line, the backup line, the undo line, one copy line per overwritten file and STATUS=OK.\"\n      - \"A nonzero pointer-sync line is the one verdict the run leaves unresolved: the generator rewrites an existing .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md and never creates a missing one, so a repository without that file ends with exit 1 and the mirror still missing. Keep the line as printed, render it in the result's Pointer sync: field, never list .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md in Files changed on the strength of the allowlist that names it, and render a Next: line naming /doctor:runtime-mirrors, whose rows list each generated mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker. The repair chain for the pointer file itself is the presentation's troubleshooting row for A10, because that route does not check it. A repo-rules line that reports an error belongs in Router: the same way.\"\n      - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line or a `foreign:` line. The engine restored from the backup by itself unless it printed `nothing was restored`, and kept the backup. Quote the lines the proof named, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it when the restore ran. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step.\"\n      - \"An allowlist refusal exits 2 before a backup exists, because every path the run would touch is resolved before the first byte. Quote the message and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n\n  phase_5_reread:\n    purpose: \"Prove the written repository reads back through the read-only engine\"\n    activities:\n      - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs once, with --root \\\"{root}\\\" when this run was pointed at another repository, and read the twelve rows against the plan's claims: the block the plan composed is the block on disk, and the paths the apply printed as written are the paths the check reads.\"\n      - \"The engine prints its own check-after line at the end of a successful apply. Keep that line and the re-read beside each other: two readings of the same tree disagreeing is a failure, not a warning.\"\n      - \"A row that still reports FINDING after a clean write is not a failed embed: the write completed and the row names a different requirement, so report it as the next step and keep the result at STATUS=OK.\"\n      - \"When the re-read cannot run at all, report its message, keep the write result, and name the missing check as the next step. Never report an embed as verified when the re-read never answered.\"\n\n  phase_6_report:\n    purpose: \"Summarize the run and hand the way back to the operator\"\n    activities:\n      - \"When the write ran and read back, render the presentation contract's embedded result with the paths the engine wrote or removed, the pointer-sync and repo-rules lines as they printed, the backup folder, the re-read verdict, the undo block the engine printed and the next line those lines name.\"\n      - \"Print the engine's undo block exactly as the apply printed it: its Undo: line, the restore command it names and the copy line per overwritten file, in that order and with no path shortened. Never compose an undo of this route's own and never run it here. Never run the undo inside this route.\"\n      - \"A no answered a question: render the cancelled result naming what was declined, state Changed: none and end with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled.\"\n      - \"A dry run: render the dry-run result with the plan, the digest and the dry-run line, and end with STATUS=OK.\"\n      - \"NOTHING TO DO: render the unchanged result with the engine's notes and STATUS=OK.\"\n      - \"A refusal, a missing asset, a dropped line or a digest mismatch stopped the run: render the failure result naming the phase and the engine's code, with STATUS=FAIL.\"\n      - \"End by saying the operator commits the written files themselves; this route stages and commits nothing.\"\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"      - \"Exit 0 with NOTHING TO DO means the repository is already in its target state, which the engine prints without a plan. Render the presentation contract's unchanged result with the engine's own notes, ask nothing, write nothing and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK.\"\n      - \"A finding line that says the composed document is past the byte ceiling is a finding rather than a refusal: every carried line is kept, because preservation outranks the budget. Show it with the plan and let the operator decide. A run whose composition drops a line refuses instead, exits 1 and writes nothing; print the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL and stop.\"\n      - \"If dry_run is true, render the presentation contract's dry-run result from the plan's own lines, print the dry-run line and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK. A dry run asks nothing and writes nothing, so it runs no question and no apply.\"\n      - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing manifest, a symlinked root document, a symlinked REPO RULES.md or Cursor mirror the run would write, or one of the two markers present without the other. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:agents-md embed), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n\n  phase_3_approval:\n    purpose: \"Ask the one embed question against the plan on screen, and write only after its yes\"\n    activities:\n      - \"Ask the embed question once, in the presentation contract's wording, naming the files the plan will create, replace or remove, the backup folder, the router rows the plan would add and the plan digest. The operator answers about the plan the operator has just read, which is this run's plan.\"\n      - \"Any answer other than yes is a no: print the cancelled result naming the declined embed, state Changed: none, and end with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled. Nothing is written.\"\n      - \"Never default an answer, never carry an approval from an earlier run, and never accept a digest the operator has not seen. Phase 4 runs only after this phase's yes.\"\n\n  phase_4_write:\n    purpose: \"Write the approved composition and nothing else, only after the embed yes\"\n    activities:\n      - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs apply --plan-digest \\\"{plan_digest}\\\" with exactly the flags the plan ran with: --root \\\"{root}\\\" when it was given, --keep-claude-md or --remove-claude-md as approved, and --create-router when it was approved. Run it only after the embed yes.\"\n      - \"Exit 2 with a message that the plan digest does not match the composition now means the tree changed after the plan, so nothing was written. Quote the engine's message, offer the plan again against the current tree, and end with STATUS=FAIL. Never retry the apply with a recomposed digest of your own: the point of the digest is that the approved bytes are the written bytes.\"\n      - \"Exit 0 means the write ran. Keep exactly the lines the engine printed: its apply line, one wrote or removed line per path, the pointer-sync line, the repo-rules line after a router write, the preservation line, the check-after line, the backup line, the undo line, one copy line per overwritten file and STATUS=OK.\"\n      - \"A nonzero pointer-sync line is the one verdict the run leaves unresolved: the generator rewrites an existing .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md and never creates a missing one, so a repository without that file ends with exit 1 and the mirror still missing. Keep the line as printed, render it in the result's Pointer sync: field, never list .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md in Files changed on the strength of the allowlist that names it, and render a Next: line naming /doctor:runtime-mirrors, whose rows list each generated mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker. The repair chain for the pointer file itself is the presentation's troubleshooting row for A10, because that route does not check it. A repo-rules line that reports an error belongs in Router: the same way.\"\n      - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line or a `foreign:` line. The engine restored from the backup by itself unless it printed `nothing was restored`, and kept the backup. Quote the lines the proof named, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it when the restore ran. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step.\"\n      - \"An allowlist refusal exits 2 before a backup exists, because every path the run would touch is resolved before the first byte. Quote the message and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n\n  phase_5_reread:\n    purpose: \"Prove the written repository reads back through the read-only engine\"\n    activities:\n      - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs once, with --root \\\"{root}\\\" when this run was pointed at another repository, and read the twelve rows against the plan's claims: the block the plan composed is the block on disk, and the paths the apply printed as written are the paths the check reads.\"\n      - \"The engine prints its own check-after line at the end of a successful apply. Keep that line and the re-read beside each other: two readings of the same tree disagreeing is a failure, not a warning.\"\n      - \"A row that still reports FINDING after a clean write is not a failed embed: the write completed and the row names a different requirement, so report it as the next step and keep the result at STATUS=OK.\"\n      - \"When the re-read cannot run at all, report its message, keep the write result, and name the missing check as the next step. Never report an embed as verified when the re-read never answered.\"\n\n  phase_6_report:\n    purpose: \"Summarize the run and hand the way back to the operator\"\n    activities:\n      - \"When the write ran and read back, render the presentation contract's embedded result with the paths the engine wrote or removed, the pointer-sync and repo-rules lines as they printed, the backup folder, the re-read verdict, the undo block the engine printed and the next line those lines name.\"\n      - \"Print the engine's undo block exactly as the apply printed it: its Undo: line, the restore command it names and the copy line per overwritten file, in that order and with no path shortened. Never compose an undo of this route's own and never run it here. Never run the undo inside this route.\"\n      - \"A no answered a question: render the cancelled result naming what was declined, state Changed: none and end with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled.\"\n      - \"A dry run: render the dry-run result with the plan, the digest and the dry-run line, and end with STATUS=OK.\"\n      - \"NOTHING TO DO: render the unchanged result with the engine's notes and STATUS=OK.\"\n      - \"A refusal, a missing asset, a dropped line or a digest mismatch stopped the run: render the failure result naming the phase and the engine's code, with STATUS=FAIL.\"\n      - \"End by saying the operator commits the written files themselves; this route stages and commits nothing.\"\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '84,125p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570615206,"end":1794570615489}}}}
