 | `Only one target may be bound.` then `Try: /doctor:agents-md check [--json] [--root <dir>] for check, /doctor:agents-md embed [--dry-run] for embed, /doctor:agents-md restore --run=<dir> for restore` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"too_many_arguments\"` |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:16:| `restore` with no run directory | `Restore needs --run=<dir>, the backup directory one apply printed.` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"missing_run_dir\"` |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:17:| An engine invoked with a subcommand or option it does not take | `USAGE: [the engine's first message line]` then the engine's usage block, exit 2. The workflow only ever runs the documented calls, so this is the engine's own contract rather than a route the operator reaches |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:41:On any other response, re-emit the menu once. On a second invalid response, return `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_selection\"`.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:253:STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[code]\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:11:| The first token is not a target | `Unknown target: [target]` then `/doctor:agents-md runs check. Try: /doctor:agents-md menu` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_target\"` |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:12:| A flag none of the three targets accepts | `Unknown argument: [argument]` then `check accepts --json and --root <dir>; embed accepts --dry-run, --root <dir>, --plan-digest <digest>, --keep-claude-md, --remove-claude-md and --create-router; restore accepts --run <dir>, --yes and --dry-run.` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:13:| A flag another target owns |