{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570637300,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4becc8f001yZQXMt4VhiGgDC","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4beb3f3001WzuA0Wt8DwcrOQ","type":"tool","id":"call_726089edabac4edda476e4a9","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"wc -l .skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md; grep -n \"STATUS\\|apply\\|exit\" .skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md | head -30"},"output":"      90 .skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md\n38:- `--plan-digest` takes the digest the same run's plan printed, and it is the only way `embed` writes: the workflow never runs `apply` without the digest its own plan printed, and never runs a writing target without its yes.\n58:| `--plan-digest <digest>` | `embed` | The digest the plan printed; the apply refuses any bytes it does not match |\n62:| `--run <dir>` | `restore` | The backup directory one apply printed, whose `manifest.json` records what to put back |\n85:4. The plan prints the plan digest, and the run shows that line in full immediately above the question. The digest the operator reads is the digest the apply repeats, so nothing else may stand in for it. With `--dry-run` the run ends here: the plan and its digest are shown, the dry-run line is printed and nothing is asked and nothing is written.\n87:6. `embed` runs `agents-md-embed.cjs apply --plan-digest <digest>` with the same flags, only after the embed yes. The engine recomposes, refuses a digest that no longer matches and writes nothing in that case, backs up every path it will touch, writes only inside its own allowlist, then proves the composition against the bytes on disk. A dropped line restores from the backup automatically.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"      90 .skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md\n38:- `--plan-digest` takes the digest the same run's plan printed, and it is the only way `embed` writes: the workflow never runs `apply` without the digest its own plan printed, and never runs a writing target without its yes.\n58:| `--plan-digest <digest>` | `embed` | The digest the plan printed; the apply refuses any bytes it does not match |\n62:| `--run <dir>` | `restore` | The backup directory one apply printed, whose `manifest.json` records what to put back |\n85:4. The plan prints the plan digest, and the run shows that line in full immediately above the question. The digest the operator reads is the digest the apply repeats, so nothing else may stand in for it. With `--dry-run` the run ends here: the plan and its digest are shown, the dry-run line is printed and nothing is asked and nothing is written.\n87:6. `embed` runs `agents-md-embed.cjs apply --plan-digest <digest>` with the same flags, only after the embed yes. The engine recomposes, refuses a digest that no longer matches and writes nothing in that case, backs up every path it will touch, writes only inside its own allowlist, then proves the composition against the bytes on disk. A dropped line restores from the backup automatically.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"wc -l .skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md; grep -n \\\"STATUS\\\\|apply\\\\|exit\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570636431,"end":1794570637300}}}}
