{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570650640,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4bf0249001tyMbkbNHFDysjZ","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4bef4ab001T78uTnk6GOxR89","type":"tool","id":"call_bddcd2309f3440f3b1cf0e00","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":160,"offset":303,"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md, lines 303-462\n303: - **iter5-P2-holdout-secondary-split-publication** `rows[row.id]` at `:537` writes every row. The committed baseline holds 176 rows, of which 44 have ids marked holdout (ids counted, no prompt text read). `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:91-107` compares them all and tells the developer to recapture. `holdout-independent.vitest.ts:5-18` names this split a secondary signal, while `spec.md:144` still uses it as acceptance evidence. Test: an assertion that no baseline row id belongs to the holdout split finds 44 today and 0 after.\n304: - **iter1-P2-readme-inventory-drift** The folder holds 14 code files (13 `.mjs` and one `.py`) against \"9\" at `:29`. It held 8 before the range. Test: a doc check comparing the count with the folder fails today.\n305: - **iter3-P2-readme-restore-exit3** `EXIT_HEAD_MOVED = 3` (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:69`) and the head-moved branch skips the restore (`:1032-1037`). The README row at `:113` lists only exit 2 and an unconditional restore. Test: a doc check that the README names exit 3 fails today.\n306: - **R1-P2-004** On an open failure (`devin.mjs:399-404`) or a projection failure (`:419-420`, `:438-440`) the loader returns `store_unreadable` without trying `loadTranscript` (`:447`). This matches the reader README's code table, so it is a design gap. Test: a corrupt `sessions.db` beside an intact transcript returns `store_unreadable` today and `ok` after.\n307: - **R1-P2-003** `dsh.mjs:195` keeps a record only for `source.kind === 'user'`. The injected list added in this range files a sourceless message as `unknown` (`:244-256`), which the reader README documents at `:36`. Whether DSH ever emits a sourceless operator message is not shown. Test: a sourceless `user/message` lands in `injected` with source `unknown`. It passes today and pins the documented rule.\n308: - **R1-P2-002--fabc628596e7** `claude.mjs:213` records `containment.path` and `:217` opens `transcriptPath`. For a link both name the same file, so the two can differ only if the path is swapped between check and open inside the user's own store. The lineage's claim that `pi.mjs` already closes the gap is wrong: it also reads `filePath` after the guard (`pi.mjs:245-256`). Test: no deterministic failing test, because the gap is a race.\n309: - **R4-P2-001--09ff48e9a0b9** `capabilities` (`index.mjs:28-65`) spells seven runtimes and no test compares it with `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`. Today the two sets agree. Test: the added comparison passes today and fails the day a runtime is added to one list only.\n310: - **R2-P2-002** `stdout += chunk` with no ceiling (`subprocess.ts:238-243`), while the hook fallback caps at 1 MiB (`skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:92`, `:214-218`). Only the timeout bounds it. Test: a fake child writing 2 MiB yields 2 MiB today and at most the cap after.\n311: - **iter4-P2-bench-runtime-matrix-incomplete** Run with `SPECKIT_RUN_BENCHES=true`, the bench file failed one of four tests with `TypeError: Cannot convert undefined or null to object` at `:95` (exit 1). The runtime tuple already held seven values before the range, when the matrix had three, so the gap predates the packet. Test: the bench file itself fails today and passes after.\n312: - **R3-P2-001--0e0d904eb571** `counts.typescriptActive` is 46 and 46 entries carry `embeddingText` in `command-bridges.generated.json`. Both 45 sentences came from the range. Test: a doc check against `counts.typescriptActive` fails today.\n313: - **R3-P2-002--5522ea1fe8dd** `hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` ships a DSH adapter and predates the range. The sentence at `:142` names five adapters plus the plugin. Test: a doc check that every adapter folder under `hooks/` is named fails today.\n314: - **R3-P2-002--ecbea1260371** The four-field recommendation contract at `:41-43` is accurate, since the output carries no `mutating`. The defect is `:45`, which gives the row shape as `{ command, policy?, ownerSkillId }` while `command-attach.ts:51` adds `mutating`, the field `render.ts:233` reads. Test: a doc check that `:45` names every `CommandRow` field fails today.\n315: - **Q2 (queued item ii)** `advisor-recommend.md:45` says the compiled-route attach takes its policy from `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]`. The code reads `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy` (`advisor-recommend.ts:478`). Test: the doc check above, extended to the policy source, fails today.\n316: - **R4-P2-003** The Gate 2 direct call passes the prompt in argv. `skill-advisor-cli.ts:391-397` already accepts `--json -` and reads stdin. Test: a doc check that the example uses `--json -` fails today.\n317: - **iter3-P2-phase007-open-evidence** The phase map shows 007 In Progress while 010 to 013 are Complete (`spec.md:120-125`). Phase 007 has 25 open tasks and its summary says \"Not completed\" (`007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/implementation-summary.md:49`). Test: `validate.sh --strict` on the parent reports the open phase today.\n318: \n319: ### 3.5 Refuted finding\n320: \n321: **R3-P2-001--16e5737e0e56**, `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:176`. The finding says the brief layer never reads `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS`. The brief calls `runAdvisorSubprocess` with `timeoutMs: options.subprocessTimeoutMs` (`skill-advisor-brief.ts:519-522`). `runAdvisorSubprocess` falls back to `defaultTimeoutMs()`, which reads that variable, whenever the option is unset (`subprocess.ts:118-120`, `:298`). Only the Claude hook passes its own value (`hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:352`). The document's list of consumers is accurate for the brief path.\n322: \n323: ---\n324: \n325: ## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n326: \n327: Every group owns its files alone, so the groups can run in parallel. The safety lane goes first. Each finding gets one test that fails before its fix and passes after, as listed in section 3.\n328: \n329: 1. **WG1 Embed engine write safety (safety lane).** DR1-P1-001, DR4-P1-001, DR4-P2-001 and DR1-P2-003. Files: `agents-md-embed.cjs`, its test file and `doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml` (give the new \"undone\" exit its own row in phase 4).\n330: 2. **WG2 Attach-path guards (safety lane).** R2-P2-001, R1-P2-001, R1-P2-002--95282927956e, R4-P2-001--d1528b81a2ca and R4-P2-002--828881666f76. Files: `command-attach.ts`, `scorer/fusion.ts`, `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `command-bridges/README.md` and a new `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`. Move `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` into the import-free `command-attach.ts` and import it in `fusion.ts`, so one pattern serves both paths. Delete `COMMAND_POLICIES` at its emitter and regenerate. A third copy of the no-edit pattern sits in `scorer/text.ts:148`, which this group leaves alone and records.\n331: 3. **WG3 Renderer contract and test isolation (safety lane).** R1-P2-005, R2-P2-003, R4-P2-002--de3d8b259d8e and Q1. Files: `render.ts`, `command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`, `hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` and `render-child-session.vitest.ts`.\n332: 4. **WG4 Behaviour runner containment (safety lane).** iter5-P2-credential-hardening-allowlist, iter2-P2-arena-precondition-unverified and iter4-P2-g2-label-grammar-duplication. Files: `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs` and a new `tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`.\n333: 5. **WG5 AGENTS.md check truth.** DR1-P2-001, DR1-P2-002, DR3-P2-001, DR5-P2-003 and DR3-P2-004. Files: `agents-md-check.cjs`, its test file and `scripts/README.markdown`.\n334: 6. **WG6 Hook check scripts.** DR5-P2-001, DR5-P2-002 and the script half of DR3-P2-002 (the repair line text is fixed in section 3.4). Files: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`, `hook-wiring-check.cjs` and their two test files.\n335: 7. **WG7 Doctor workflow contracts.** The workflow half of DR3-P2-002, DR3-P2-003, DR2-P2-003 and Q3. Files: `doctor-setup.yaml`, `setup.md`, `doctor-setup-presentation.txt`, `doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml`, `doctor-symlink-check.yaml` and a new `tests/doctor-setup-contract.test.cjs`.\n336: 8. **WG8 Install guide and embedder host.** DR2-P2-001 and DR2-P2-002. Files: `doctor-install-presentation.txt`, `doctor-install.yaml`, `doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`, `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` and `skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs`.\n337: 9. **WG9 Holdout rows out of the baseline.** iter5-P2-holdout-secondary-split-publication. Files: `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `command-routing-baseline.json` (recaptured with `--write`) and `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`. The worker counts holdout rows by id and split only and never prints their prompt text.\n338: 10. **WG10 Routing-accuracy README.** iter1-P2-readme-inventory-drift, iter3-P2-readme-restore-exit3 and iter1-P2-offer-reached-unknown. File: `routing-accuracy/README.md`.\n339: 11. **WG11 Session readers.** R1-P2-004, R1-P2-003, R1-P2-002--fabc628596e7 and R4-P2-001--09ff48e9a0b9. Files: the claude, devin, dsh, pi and index readers, the readers' README, their tests and `advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`.\n340: 12. **WG12 Subprocess cap and bench.** R2-P2-002 and iter4-P2-bench-runtime-matrix-incomplete. Files: `subprocess.ts`, a new `tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` and the bench file.\n341: 13. **WG13 Advisor docs.** R3-P2-001--0e0d904eb571, R3-P2-002--5522ea1fe8dd, R3-P2-002--ecbea1260371 and Q2. Files: the skill `README.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md` and the two feature-catalog pages. The wording follows WG2's decision to delete `COMMAND_POLICIES`, which is fixed here, so the group does not wait for WG2.\n342: 14. **WG14 Operator and coordinator items.** R4-P2-003 waits for the operator, because `AGENTS.md` is the shared framework document mirrored to every runtime. If its Gate 2 section is a shipped body, the agents-md manifest needs regenerating with it. iter3-P2-phase007-open-evidence belongs to the coordinator.\n343: \n344: ---\n345: \n346: ## 5. Spec Seed\n347: \n348: - A failed write inside an embed apply restores from the backup, prints the backup and undo lines and exits with a code the workflow reads as undone.\n349: - Embed refuses a symlinked router or Cursor mirror with the same rule it applies to a symlinked root document.\n350: - A no-edit prompt attaches no mutating command on either the scorer path or the hub route path, through one shared pattern.\n351: - A typed command is matched only outside a file name. The deep-loop gate opens only for the typed command it attaches.\n352: - `TRACKED_COMMANDS` is the one attach-path policy table and every doc says so.\n353: - The renderer's tests set or clear `AI_SESSION_CHILD` themselves.\n354: - A live behaviour arm starts only in a marked arena and with an allowlisted child environment.\n355: - The published command baseline carries no per-row outcome for a holdout row.\n356: - Doctor checks never count a known gap as expected, never read a mention as a wired hook and always print the repair they promise.\n357: - The setup advisor leg states when hook health is not recorded.\n358: \n359: ---\n360: \n361: ## 6. Plan Seed\n362: \n363: 1. Dispatch WG1, WG2, WG3 and WG4 in parallel. Each worker writes the failing test first, confirms it fails, applies the fix and confirms it passes.\n364: 2. Dispatch WG5 to WG13 in parallel under the same rule.\n365: 3. Run each touched test file alone as `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <file>` or `node --test <file>`. Run the deriver's check mode after WG2.\n366: 4. Hand WG14 to the operator (AGENTS.md) and the coordinator (phase 007 status).\n367: 5. Run a second `/deep:review` fan-out over the remediation diff with the same four lineages and the 0.10 threshold. The loop counts as converged only when every lineage stops below the threshold.\n368: \n369: ---\n370: \n371: ## 7. Traceability Status\n372: \n373: ### Core protocols\n374: \n375: | Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n376: |---|---|---|\n377: | `spec_code` | partial | Twelve findings are docs that disagree with code (R3-P2-001--0e0d904eb571, R3-P2-002--5522ea1fe8dd, R3-P2-002--ecbea1260371, Q2, iter1-P2-readme-inventory-drift, iter3-P2-readme-restore-exit3, iter1-P2-offer-reached-unknown, DR3-P2-004, DR2-P2-003, DR3-P2-002, DR3-P2-003 and R4-P2-003). One claimed drift was refuted. |\n378: | `checklist_evidence` | partial | The phased parent has no root checklist. Phase 007 holds 25 open tasks while later phases are Complete (iter3-P2-phase007-open-evidence). |\n379: | `AC_COVERAGE` | exempt | The parent has no `acceptance-criteria.md`. Child phases own theirs. |\n380: \n381: ### Overlay protocols\n382: \n383: | Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n384: |---|---|---|\n385: | `skill_agent` | pass | The scorer-attach lineage matched 36 doctor bridge owners to their router tags with no mismatch. Not re-run here. |\n386: | `agent_cross_runtime` | partial | dsh has an advisor prompt adapter but no install row in `symlink-manifest.json` and no name in `ARCHITECTURE.md:142`. The per-runtime behaviour proof (phase 007) is open. |\n387: | `feature_catalog_code` | partial | `advisor-recommend.md:45` names the wrong policy table and an incomplete row shape. `command-meaning-matching.md:26` gives 45 rows where the artifact holds 46. |\n388: | `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | No lineage reviewed a playbook file against its capability. This synthesis added none. |\n389: \n390: Resource Map Coverage Gate: skipped. `resource-map.md` does not exist in the spec folder, so `resource_map_present` is false in the root config. No lineage emitted a `resource-map.md` either.\n391: \n392: ---\n393: \n394: ## 8. Deferred Items\n395: \n396: - **R2-P1-001 (resolved by the render-hooks-plugin lineage).** The child downgrade still has no per-request input: `SkillAdvisorBriefOptions` carries no `childSession`, so a host that serves a child in-process without setting `AI_SESSION_CHILD` renders a parent brief. The lineage closed it at P1 because the behaviour matches `skill-advisor-hook.md:39`. It reopens as P1 the moment a host is shown dispatching a child in-process.\n397: - **`run` commands that write.** `/doctor:deep-loop` and `/doctor:speckit` are `run` with class `add-only` (`command-attach.ts:80`, `:105`), so they start without asking and add files. The scorer-attach lineage summary said no `run` row writes. Whether `add-only` under `run` is intended belongs in a decision, not a fix.\n398: - **dsh install path.** `/doctor:install` cannot link a dsh runtime because `symlink-manifest.json` has no `dsh` row. Adding one is a feature decision.\n399: - **DR1-P1-001 reach on sandboxed runtimes.** If a supported runtime's sandbox denies a write to one of the allowlisted paths on a default install, the mid-apply fault becomes reachable on a default path and the finding returns to P1. Not verified here.\n400: - **R1-P2-003 reach.** Whether DSH ever emits an operator message with no `source` is not shown by any fixture or store read here.\n401: - **Third no-edit pattern.** `scorer/text.ts:148` holds a copy of the no-edit wording beside `fusion.ts:677`. WG2 records it and leaves it.\n402: \n403: ---\n404: \n405: ## Dimension Expansion Map\n406: \n407: - All four lineages covered all four dimensions (`dimensionCoverage` true for correctness, security, traceability and maintainability in every lineage registry).\n408: - Divergence state is empty in every lineage registry: no pivot started, completed or failed, no audited override, no saturated direction and no remaining frontier recorded.\n409: - Selected directions in the lineages: per-runtime branch logic, mutating-command safety, holdout hygiene and doc-code agreement, plus filesystem write containment in doctor-install.\n410: - This map records breadth only and changes no verdict.\n411: \n412: ---\n413: \n414: ## Search Ledger\n415: \n416: | Lineage | searchCoverage rows | candidateCoverage rows | searchDebt | ruledOutCandidates | cleanSearchProof |\n417: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n418: | scorer-attach | 6 | 5 | 0 | 14 | 14 |\n419: | render-hooks-plugin | 6 | 5 | 0 | 10 | 10 |\n420: | accuracy-runner | 6 | 5 | 0 | 9 | 9 |\n421: | doctor-install | 6 | 5 | 0 | 5 | 5 |\n422: \n423: hasSearchDebt: false. The graph was unavailable in every lineage, which recorded `graphless_fallback` with direct reads.\n424: \n425: ---\n426: \n427: ## 9. Audit Appendix\n428: \n429: ### Convergence\n430: \n431: Confirmed from each lineage's `deep-review-state.jsonl` (`newFindingsRatio` per iteration) and its `synthesis_complete` event.\n432: \n433: | Lineage | Iterations | Stop reason | Novelty per iteration | Last ratio against 0.10 |\n434: |---|---|---|---|---|\n435: | scorer-attach | 5 | converged | 1.00, 0.33, 0.40, 0.29, 0.00 | below |\n436: | render-hooks-plugin | 5 | maxIterationsReached | 1.00, 1.00, 0.33, 0.23, 0.15 | above |\n437: | accuracy-runner | 5 | maxIterationsReached | 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 0.11 | above |\n438: | doctor-install | 5 | maxIterationsReached | 1.00, 0.27, 0.21, 0.29, 0.125 | above |\n439: \n440: Three lineages stopped at their cap above the 0.10 threshold. The fan-out therefore did not converge. A second review pass after remediation is required before the loop counts as converged.\n441: \n442: ### Dimension order per lineage\n443: \n444: - scorer-attach, render-hooks-plugin and accuracy-runner: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability, then one pass over all four.\n445: - doctor-install: correctness twice, then traceability, security and maintainability.\n446: \n447: ### Probes run in this synthesis\n448: \n449: All read-only or confined to temporary directories that were removed.\n450: \n451: - `agents-md-embed.cjs` in-process on fixture trees: a write hook throwing on the second write, an in-root router link, an in-root mirror link to a CI file, a router linked to `AGENTS.md` and a router linked outside the root.\n452: - `agents-md-check.cjs --json` on a fixture with no `CLAUDE.md` and a linked `.codex/AGENTS.md`.\n453: - `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root --json` and `hook-wiring-check.cjs` on a settings file that only echoes the marker.\n454: - `command-attach.ts` through `node --experimental-strip-types`: `attachCommand`, `typedCommandIn`, `typedCommandForTop`, the hub row lookup and the policy table comparison.\n455: - `compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt-stdin` on four no-edit prompts.\n456: - `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend` on five no-edit prompts.\n457: - The built `render.js` with `needsMode`, child-session and `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` inputs.\n458: - `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run` on `tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` (12 passed) and on `tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` (3 passed).\n459: - The bench file with `SPECKIT_RUN_BENCHES=true` (1 of 4 failed).\n460: - `git blame` on every cited line range, with each blamed commit tested as an ancestor of `35c3188681`.\n461: \n462: ### Holdout handling\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 463]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md, lines 303-462\n303: - **iter5-P2-holdout-secondary-split-publication** `rows[row.id]` at `:537` writes every row. The committed baseline holds 176 rows, of which 44 have ids marked holdout (ids counted, no prompt text read). `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:91-107` compares them all and tells the developer to recapture. `holdout-independent.vitest.ts:5-18` names this split a secondary signal, while `spec.md:144` still uses it as acceptance evidence. Test: an assertion that no baseline row id belongs to the holdout split finds 44 today and 0 after.\n304: - **iter1-P2-readme-inventory-drift** The folder holds 14 code files (13 `.mjs` and one `.py`) against \"9\" at `:29`. It held 8 before the range. Test: a doc check comparing the count with the folder fails today.\n305: - **iter3-P2-readme-restore-exit3** `EXIT_HEAD_MOVED = 3` (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:69`) and the head-moved branch skips the restore (`:1032-1037`). The README row at `:113` lists only exit 2 and an unconditional restore. Test: a doc check that the README names exit 3 fails today.\n306: - **R1-P2-004** On an open failure (`devin.mjs:399-404`) or a projection failure (`:419-420`, `:438-440`) the loader returns `store_unreadable` without trying `loadTranscript` (`:447`). This matches the reader README's code table, so it is a design gap. Test: a corrupt `sessions.db` beside an intact transcript returns `store_unreadable` today and `ok` after.\n307: - **R1-P2-003** `dsh.mjs:195` keeps a record only for `source.kind === 'user'`. The injected list added in this range files a sourceless message as `unknown` (`:244-256`), which the reader README documents at `:36`. Whether DSH ever emits a sourceless operator message is not shown. Test: a sourceless `user/message` lands in `injected` with source `unknown`. It passes today and pins the documented rule.\n308: - **R1-P2-002--fabc628596e7** `claude.mjs:213` records `containment.path` and `:217` opens `transcriptPath`. For a link both name the same file, so the two can differ only if the path is swapped between check and open inside the user's own store. The lineage's claim that `pi.mjs` already closes the gap is wrong: it also reads `filePath` after the guard (`pi.mjs:245-256`). Test: no deterministic failing test, because the gap is a race.\n309: - **R4-P2-001--09ff48e9a0b9** `capabilities` (`index.mjs:28-65`) spells seven runtimes and no test compares it with `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`. Today the two sets agree. Test: the added comparison passes today and fails the day a runtime is added to one list only.\n310: - **R2-P2-002** `stdout += chunk` with no ceiling (`subprocess.ts:238-243`), while the hook fallback caps at 1 MiB (`skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:92`, `:214-218`). Only the timeout bounds it. Test: a fake child writing 2 MiB yields 2 MiB today and at most the cap after.\n311: - **iter4-P2-bench-runtime-matrix-incomplete** Run with `SPECKIT_RUN_BENCHES=true`, the bench file failed one of four tests with `TypeError: Cannot convert undefined or null to object` at `:95` (exit 1). The runtime tuple already held seven values before the range, when the matrix had three, so the gap predates the packet. Test: the bench file itself fails today and passes after.\n312: - **R3-P2-001--0e0d904eb571** `counts.typescriptActive` is 46 and 46 entries carry `embeddingText` in `command-bridges.generated.json`. Both 45 sentences came from the range. Test: a doc check against `counts.typescriptActive` fails today.\n313: - **R3-P2-002--5522ea1fe8dd** `hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` ships a DSH adapter and predates the range. The sentence at `:142` names five adapters plus the plugin. Test: a doc check that every adapter folder under `hooks/` is named fails today.\n314: - **R3-P2-002--ecbea1260371** The four-field recommendation contract at `:41-43` is accurate, since the output carries no `mutating`. The defect is `:45`, which gives the row shape as `{ command, policy?, ownerSkillId }` while `command-attach.ts:51` adds `mutating`, the field `render.ts:233` reads. Test: a doc check that `:45` names every `CommandRow` field fails today.\n315: - **Q2 (queued item ii)** `advisor-recommend.md:45` says the compiled-route attach takes its policy from `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]`. The code reads `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy` (`advisor-recommend.ts:478`). Test: the doc check above, extended to the policy source, fails today.\n316: - **R4-P2-003** The Gate 2 direct call passes the prompt in argv. `skill-advisor-cli.ts:391-397` already accepts `--json -` and reads stdin. Test: a doc check that the example uses `--json -` fails today.\n317: - **iter3-P2-phase007-open-evidence** The phase map shows 007 In Progress while 010 to 013 are Complete (`spec.md:120-125`). Phase 007 has 25 open tasks and its summary says \"Not completed\" (`007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/implementation-summary.md:49`). Test: `validate.sh --strict` on the parent reports the open phase today.\n318: \n319: ### 3.5 Refuted finding\n320: \n321: **R3-P2-001--16e5737e0e56**, `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:176`. The finding says the brief layer never reads `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS`. The brief calls `runAdvisorSubprocess` with `timeoutMs: options.subprocessTimeoutMs` (`skill-advisor-brief.ts:519-522`). `runAdvisorSubprocess` falls back to `defaultTimeoutMs()`, which reads that variable, whenever the option is unset (`subprocess.ts:118-120`, `:298`). Only the Claude hook passes its own value (`hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:352`). The document's list of consumers is accurate for the brief path.\n322: \n323: ---\n324: \n325: ## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n326: \n327: Every group owns its files alone, so the groups can run in parallel. The safety lane goes first. Each finding gets one test that fails before its fix and passes after, as listed in section 3.\n328: \n329: 1. **WG1 Embed engine write safety (safety lane).** DR1-P1-001, DR4-P1-001, DR4-P2-001 and DR1-P2-003. Files: `agents-md-embed.cjs`, its test file and `doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml` (give the new \"undone\" exit its own row in phase 4).\n330: 2. **WG2 Attach-path guards (safety lane).** R2-P2-001, R1-P2-001, R1-P2-002--95282927956e, R4-P2-001--d1528b81a2ca and R4-P2-002--828881666f76. Files: `command-attach.ts`, `scorer/fusion.ts`, `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `command-bridges/README.md` and a new `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`. Move `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` into the import-free `command-attach.ts` and import it in `fusion.ts`, so one pattern serves both paths. Delete `COMMAND_POLICIES` at its emitter and regenerate. A third copy of the no-edit pattern sits in `scorer/text.ts:148`, which this group leaves alone and records.\n331: 3. **WG3 Renderer contract and test isolation (safety lane).** R1-P2-005, R2-P2-003, R4-P2-002--de3d8b259d8e and Q1. Files: `render.ts`, `command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`, `hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` and `render-child-session.vitest.ts`.\n332: 4. **WG4 Behaviour runner containment (safety lane).** iter5-P2-credential-hardening-allowlist, iter2-P2-arena-precondition-unverified and iter4-P2-g2-label-grammar-duplication. Files: `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs` and a new `tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`.\n333: 5. **WG5 AGENTS.md check truth.** DR1-P2-001, DR1-P2-002, DR3-P2-001, DR5-P2-003 and DR3-P2-004. Files: `agents-md-check.cjs`, its test file and `scripts/README.markdown`.\n334: 6. **WG6 Hook check scripts.** DR5-P2-001, DR5-P2-002 and the script half of DR3-P2-002 (the repair line text is fixed in section 3.4). Files: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`, `hook-wiring-check.cjs` and their two test files.\n335: 7. **WG7 Doctor workflow contracts.** The workflow half of DR3-P2-002, DR3-P2-003, DR2-P2-003 and Q3. Files: `doctor-setup.yaml`, `setup.md`, `doctor-setup-presentation.txt`, `doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml`, `doctor-symlink-check.yaml` and a new `tests/doctor-setup-contract.test.cjs`.\n336: 8. **WG8 Install guide and embedder host.** DR2-P2-001 and DR2-P2-002. Files: `doctor-install-presentation.txt`, `doctor-install.yaml`, `doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`, `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` and `skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs`.\n337: 9. **WG9 Holdout rows out of the baseline.** iter5-P2-holdout-secondary-split-publication. Files: `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `command-routing-baseline.json` (recaptured with `--write`) and `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`. The worker counts holdout rows by id and split only and never prints their prompt text.\n338: 10. **WG10 Routing-accuracy README.** iter1-P2-readme-inventory-drift, iter3-P2-readme-restore-exit3 and iter1-P2-offer-reached-unknown. File: `routing-accuracy/README.md`.\n339: 11. **WG11 Session readers.** R1-P2-004, R1-P2-003, R1-P2-002--fabc628596e7 and R4-P2-001--09ff48e9a0b9. Files: the claude, devin, dsh, pi and index readers, the readers' README, their tests and `advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`.\n340: 12. **WG12 Subprocess cap and bench.** R2-P2-002 and iter4-P2-bench-runtime-matrix-incomplete. Files: `subprocess.ts`, a new `tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` and the bench file.\n341: 13. **WG13 Advisor docs.** R3-P2-001--0e0d904eb571, R3-P2-002--5522ea1fe8dd, R3-P2-002--ecbea1260371 and Q2. Files: the skill `README.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md` and the two feature-catalog pages. The wording follows WG2's decision to delete `COMMAND_POLICIES`, which is fixed here, so the group does not wait for WG2.\n342: 14. **WG14 Operator and coordinator items.** R4-P2-003 waits for the operator, because `AGENTS.md` is the shared framework document mirrored to every runtime. If its Gate 2 section is a shipped body, the agents-md manifest needs regenerating with it. iter3-P2-phase007-open-evidence belongs to the coordinator.\n343: \n344: ---\n345: \n346: ## 5. Spec Seed\n347: \n348: - A failed write inside an embed apply restores from the backup, prints the backup and undo lines and exits with a code the workflow reads as undone.\n349: - Embed refuses a symlinked router or Cursor mirror with the same rule it applies to a symlinked root document.\n350: - A no-edit prompt attaches no mutating command on either the scorer path or the hub route path, through one shared pattern.\n351: - A typed command is matched only outside a file name. The deep-loop gate opens only for the typed command it attaches.\n352: - `TRACKED_COMMANDS` is the one attach-path policy table and every doc says so.\n353: - The renderer's tests set or clear `AI_SESSION_CHILD` themselves.\n354: - A live behaviour arm starts only in a marked arena and with an allowlisted child environment.\n355: - The published command baseline carries no per-row outcome for a holdout row.\n356: - Doctor checks never count a known gap as expected, never read a mention as a wired hook and always print the repair they promise.\n357: - The setup advisor leg states when hook health is not recorded.\n358: \n359: ---\n360: \n361: ## 6. Plan Seed\n362: \n363: 1. Dispatch WG1, WG2, WG3 and WG4 in parallel. Each worker writes the failing test first, confirms it fails, applies the fix and confirms it passes.\n364: 2. Dispatch WG5 to WG13 in parallel under the same rule.\n365: 3. Run each touched test file alone as `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <file>` or `node --test <file>`. Run the deriver's check mode after WG2.\n366: 4. Hand WG14 to the operator (AGENTS.md) and the coordinator (phase 007 status).\n367: 5. Run a second `/deep:review` fan-out over the remediation diff with the same four lineages and the 0.10 threshold. The loop counts as converged only when every lineage stops below the threshold.\n368: \n369: ---\n370: \n371: ## 7. Traceability Status\n372: \n373: ### Core protocols\n374: \n375: | Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n376: |---|---|---|\n377: | `spec_code` | partial | Twelve findings are docs that disagree with code (R3-P2-001--0e0d904eb571, R3-P2-002--5522ea1fe8dd, R3-P2-002--ecbea1260371, Q2, iter1-P2-readme-inventory-drift, iter3-P2-readme-restore-exit3, iter1-P2-offer-reached-unknown, DR3-P2-004, DR2-P2-003, DR3-P2-002, DR3-P2-003 and R4-P2-003). One claimed drift was refuted. |\n378: | `checklist_evidence` | partial | The phased parent has no root checklist. Phase 007 holds 25 open tasks while later phases are Complete (iter3-P2-phase007-open-evidence). |\n379: | `AC_COVERAGE` | exempt | The parent has no `acceptance-criteria.md`. Child phases own theirs. |\n380: \n381: ### Overlay protocols\n382: \n383: | Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n384: |---|---|---|\n385: | `skill_agent` | pass | The scorer-attach lineage matched 36 doctor bridge owners to their router tags with no mismatch. Not re-run here. |\n386: | `agent_cross_runtime` | partial | dsh has an advisor prompt adapter but no install row in `symlink-manifest.json` and no name in `ARCHITECTURE.md:142`. The per-runtime behaviour proof (phase 007) is open. |\n387: | `feature_catalog_code` | partial | `advisor-recommend.md:45` names the wrong policy table and an incomplete row shape. `command-meaning-matching.md:26` gives 45 rows where the artifact holds 46. |\n388: | `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | No lineage reviewed a playbook file against its capability. This synthesis added none. |\n389: \n390: Resource Map Coverage Gate: skipped. `resource-map.md` does not exist in the spec folder, so `resource_map_present` is false in the root config. No lineage emitted a `resource-map.md` either.\n391: \n392: ---\n393: \n394: ## 8. Deferred Items\n395: \n396: - **R2-P1-001 (resolved by the render-hooks-plugin lineage).** The child downgrade still has no per-request input: `SkillAdvisorBriefOptions` carries no `childSession`, so a host that serves a child in-process without setting `AI_SESSION_CHILD` renders a parent brief. The lineage closed it at P1 because the behaviour matches `skill-advisor-hook.md:39`. It reopens as P1 the moment a host is shown dispatching a child in-process.\n397: - **`run` commands that write.** `/doctor:deep-loop` and `/doctor:speckit` are `run` with class `add-only` (`command-attach.ts:80`, `:105`), so they start without asking and add files. The scorer-attach lineage summary said no `run` row writes. Whether `add-only` under `run` is intended belongs in a decision, not a fix.\n398: - **dsh install path.** `/doctor:install` cannot link a dsh runtime because `symlink-manifest.json` has no `dsh` row. Adding one is a feature decision.\n399: - **DR1-P1-001 reach on sandboxed runtimes.** If a supported runtime's sandbox denies a write to one of the allowlisted paths on a default install, the mid-apply fault becomes reachable on a default path and the finding returns to P1. Not verified here.\n400: - **R1-P2-003 reach.** Whether DSH ever emits an operator message with no `source` is not shown by any fixture or store read here.\n401: - **Third no-edit pattern.** `scorer/text.ts:148` holds a copy of the no-edit wording beside `fusion.ts:677`. WG2 records it and leaves it.\n402: \n403: ---\n404: \n405: ## Dimension Expansion Map\n406: \n407: - All four lineages covered all four dimensions (`dimensionCoverage` true for correctness, security, traceability and maintainability in every lineage registry).\n408: - Divergence state is empty in every lineage registry: no pivot started, completed or failed, no audited override, no saturated direction and no remaining frontier recorded.\n409: - Selected directions in the lineages: per-runtime branch logic, mutating-command safety, holdout hygiene and doc-code agreement, plus filesystem write containment in doctor-install.\n410: - This map records breadth only and changes no verdict.\n411: \n412: ---\n413: \n414: ## Search Ledger\n415: \n416: | Lineage | searchCoverage rows | candidateCoverage rows | searchDebt | ruledOutCandidates | cleanSearchProof |\n417: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n418: | scorer-attach | 6 | 5 | 0 | 14 | 14 |\n419: | render-hooks-plugin | 6 | 5 | 0 | 10 | 10 |\n420: | accuracy-runner | 6 | 5 | 0 | 9 | 9 |\n421: | doctor-install | 6 | 5 | 0 | 5 | 5 |\n422: \n423: hasSearchDebt: false. The graph was unavailable in every lineage, which recorded `graphless_fallback` with direct reads.\n424: \n425: ---\n426: \n427: ## 9. Audit Appendix\n428: \n429: ### Convergence\n430: \n431: Confirmed from each lineage's `deep-review-state.jsonl` (`newFindingsRatio` per iteration) and its `synthesis_complete` event.\n432: \n433: | Lineage | Iterations | Stop reason | Novelty per iteration | Last ratio against 0.10 |\n434: |---|---|---|---|---|\n435: | scorer-attach | 5 | converged | 1.00, 0.33, 0.40, 0.29, 0.00 | below |\n436: | render-hooks-plugin | 5 | maxIterationsReached | 1.00, 1.00, 0.33, 0.23, 0.15 | above |\n437: | accuracy-runner | 5 | maxIterationsReached | 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 0.11 | above |\n438: | doctor-install | 5 | maxIterationsReached | 1.00, 0.27, 0.21, 0.29, 0.125 | above |\n439: \n440: Three lineages stopped at their cap above the 0.10 threshold. The fan-out therefore did not converge. A second review pass after remediation is required before the loop counts as converged.\n441: \n442: ### Dimension order per lineage\n443: \n444: - scorer-attach, render-hooks-plugin and accuracy-runner: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability, then one pass over all four.\n445: - doctor-install: correctness twice, then traceability, security and maintainability.\n446: \n447: ### Probes run in this synthesis\n448: \n449: All read-only or confined to temporary directories that were removed.\n450: \n451: - `agents-md-embed.cjs` in-process on fixture trees: a write hook throwing on the second write, an in-root router link, an in-root mirror link to a CI file, a router linked to `AGENTS.md` and a router linked outside the root.\n452: - `agents-md-check.cjs --json` on a fixture with no `CLAUDE.md` and a linked `.codex/AGENTS.md`.\n453: - `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root --json` and `hook-wiring-check.cjs` on a settings file that only echoes the marker.\n454: - `command-attach.ts` through `node --experimental-strip-types`: `attachCommand`, `typedCommandIn`, `typedCommandForTop`, the hub row lookup and the policy table comparison.\n455: - `compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt-stdin` on four no-edit prompts.\n456: - `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend` on five no-edit prompts.\n457: - The built `render.js` with `needsMode`, child-session and `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` inputs.\n458: - `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run` on `tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` (12 passed) and on `tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` (3 passed).\n459: - The bench file with `SPECKIT_RUN_BENCHES=true` (1 of 4 failed).\n460: - `git blame` on every cited line range, with each blamed commit tested as an ancestor of `35c3188681`.\n461: \n462: ### Holdout handling\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 463]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":160,\"offset\":303,\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570650185,"end":1794570650640}}}}
