{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570657022,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4bf18ad002Q7j3wC3qsFEI32","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4bf0a75001gHxwBfkIo6HUgy","type":"tool","id":"call_32182dcd457f47ada91a0951","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n 'dsh\\|runtimes' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json | head -20; grep -n \"dsh\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt | head -10; grep -n \"runtimes\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml | head -10"},"output":"4:  \"runtimes\": {\n46:  runtimes: \"The runtime list, supplied with --runtimes or in the consolidated prompt; the operator can choose the runtimes already there. DSH is not offered, because the link manifest has no dsh row.\"\n58:    - \"Ask: When --root or --runtimes is missing, ask once for the target repo's absolute path, runtimes (claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, or the ones already there), link shape (auto, whole or merge) and instruction file (embed or link). Stop for the answers.\"\n59:    - \"Inspect: Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir> [--runtimes <list>] [--link-instructions] once in place. Use only the check subcommand; include --link-instructions only when the operator chose link. Render the engine's entry lines through the presentation contract.\"\n60:    - \"Checklist: Print these ordered writing steps through the presentation contract and stop; never run them. For each command, copy its mutation class verbatim from _routes.yaml and print one line explaining why: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>, with --link-instructions only when link was chosen; it shows a plan and asks before writing. 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>, only when embed was chosen. 3) /doctor:mcp install, from the Skilled checkout, to build and register Code Mode. 4) /doctor:git setup, from inside the target repo. 5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder, from inside the target repo, to set up meaning matching for commands. It shows its cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, and a no leaves a phrase-only install. 6) /doctor:setup, from inside the target repo, to confirm the result. Pass only values the operator gave.\"\n68:  --json prints one JSON object with source, root, runtimes, builds, symlink_check and steps: [{ order, command, mutating, why }], and nothing else.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4:  \"runtimes\": {\n46:  runtimes: \"The runtime list, supplied with --runtimes or in the consolidated prompt; the operator can choose the runtimes already there. DSH is not offered, because the link manifest has no dsh row.\"\n58:    - \"Ask: When --root or --runtimes is missing, ask once for the target repo's absolute path, runtimes (claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, or the ones already there), link shape (auto, whole or merge) and instruction file (embed or link). Stop for the answers.\"\n59:    - \"Inspect: Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir> [--runtimes <list>] [--link-instructions] once in place. Use only the check subcommand; include --link-instructions only when the operator chose link. Render the engine's entry lines through the presentation contract.\"\n60:    - \"Checklist: Print these ordered writing steps through the presentation contract and stop; never run them. For each command, copy its mutation class verbatim from _routes.yaml and print one line explaining why: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>, with --link-instructions only when link was chosen; it shows a plan and asks before writing. 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>, only when embed was chosen. 3) /doctor:mcp install, from the Skilled checkout, to build and register Code Mode. 4) /doctor:git setup, from inside the target repo. 5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder, from inside the target repo, to set up meaning matching for commands. It shows its cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, and a no leaves a phrase-only install. 6) /doctor:setup, from inside the target repo, to confirm the result. Pass only values the operator gave.\"\n68:  --json prints one JSON object with source, root, runtimes, builds, symlink_check and steps: [{ order, command, mutating, why }], and nothing else.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n 'dsh\\\\|runtimes' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json | head -20; grep -n \\\"dsh\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt | head -10; grep -n \\\"runtimes\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570655917,"end":1794570657022}}}}
