{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570675469,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4bf62c9001pONgze1J615FOf","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4bf314d001RaT5dVrmtHwemI","type":"tool","id":"call_4cc1ab16d1dc4259a48793bc","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"agents-md\\|doctor:setup\\|doctor:install\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md | head -20"},"output":"INSTALL-SKILLED.md:60:/doctor:setup\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:71:`/doctor:setup` also reports a delivery leg, which reads DEGRADED with the repair step when a runtime's prompt hook is missing or Codex has not approved it.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:116:Your checkout is ready once `/doctor:setup` passes. Run `/doctor:setup` again whenever something looks wrong. To use Skilled in a project of your own, pick a way in below.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:127:/doctor:install\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:148:| 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md` and leaves the CLAUDE.md pointer. Skip it if you chose `link` |\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:152:| 6 | `/doctor:setup` | your project | Confirms the whole setup works |\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:197:> **Context saves.** `/speckit:save` records your session's progress in the `specs/` folder of the repo you run it from. Run `/doctor:setup` and every save from your project, not from the checkout.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:340:| **When something looks wrong** | Run `/doctor:setup` in your project | Run `/doctor:overlay status`, then `/doctor:setup` |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:54:- `/doctor:install` sets up the embedder by default: its checklist includes `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`, which prints the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, so answering no leaves a phrase-only install.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:372:`/doctor:install` includes the embedder setup by default, and the setup itself runs as `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` from inside the target repo. The route probes `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true`, prints one plan row per missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks once before it runs anything. A no stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` and changes nothing. `--dry-run` prints the plan and stops with `STATUS=OK`. The route never installs or upgrades Ollama: it prints the install command for the operator, and the install guide owns that cost. The two health flags split the diagnosis: `includeEmbeddingsHealth` probes only the hf-local model server, while `includeSemanticHealth` reports the active embedder and probes its backend.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"INSTALL-SKILLED.md:60:/doctor:setup\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:71:`/doctor:setup` also reports a delivery leg, which reads DEGRADED with the repair step when a runtime's prompt hook is missing or Codex has not approved it.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:116:Your checkout is ready once `/doctor:setup` passes. Run `/doctor:setup` again whenever something looks wrong. To use Skilled in a project of your own, pick a way in below.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:127:/doctor:install\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:148:| 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md` and leaves the CLAUDE.md pointer. Skip it if you chose `link` |\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:152:| 6 | `/doctor:setup` | your project | Confirms the whole setup works |\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:197:> **Context saves.** `/speckit:save` records your session's progress in the `specs/` folder of the repo you run it from. Run `/doctor:setup` and every save from your project, not from the checkout.\nINSTALL-SKILLED.md:340:| **When something looks wrong** | Run `/doctor:setup` in your project | Run `/doctor:overlay status`, then `/doctor:setup` |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:54:- `/doctor:install` sets up the embedder by default: its checklist includes `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`, which prints the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, so answering no leaves a phrase-only install.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:372:`/doctor:install` includes the embedder setup by default, and the setup itself runs as `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` from inside the target repo. The route probes `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true`, prints one plan row per missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks once before it runs anything. A no stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` and changes nothing. `--dry-run` prints the plan and stops with `STATUS=OK`. The route never installs or upgrades Ollama: it prints the install command for the operator, and the install guide owns that cost. The two health flags split the diagnosis: `includeEmbeddingsHealth` probes only the hf-local model server, while `includeSemanticHealth` reports the active embedder and probes its backend.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"agents-md\\\\|doctor:setup\\\\|doctor:install\\\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570674889,"end":1794570675469}}}}
