{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570681641,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4bf7bb6001x2S2WrZrgWURN8","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4bf7046001OF435C5EvM2vZX","type":"tool","id":"call_a6baa7bf548b4a0fbbd6f75c","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":45,"offset":120,"path":"INSTALL-SKILLED.md"},"output":"Read file INSTALL-SKILLED.md, lines 120-164\n120: ## 3. LINK IT INTO YOUR PROJECT\n121: \n122: ### Step 1: Run the Install Guide\n123: \n124: Open your Skilled checkout in your runtime and run:\n125: \n126: ```\n127: /doctor:install\n128: ```\n129: \n130: It asks four questions in one prompt:\n131: \n132: 1. **Target repo:** the absolute path of your project.\n133: 2. **Runtimes:** the AI coding tools you use. Pick any of `claude`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin` and `pi`.\n134: 3. **Link shape:** choose `auto`. [What Gets Linked](#what-gets-linked) explains the shapes.\n135: 4. **Instruction file:** `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md` and leaves a one-line `CLAUDE.md` reading `@AGENTS.md`, because Claude Code reads only `CLAUDE.md`. `link` points `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` at the checkout's copies.\n136: \n137: <!-- readme-check\n138: allow-ref CLAUDE.md | the instruction file in the operator's target repo, which this checkout does not ship\n139: -->\n140: \n141: The guide writes nothing. It prints the steps below with your paths filled in.\n142: \n143: ### Step 2: Run the Printed Steps\n144: \n145: | Step | Command | Run it from | What it does |\n146: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n147: | 1 | `/doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode auto` | the checkout | Links `.skilled` and your runtime folders into the project |\n148: | 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md` and leaves the CLAUDE.md pointer. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n149: | 3 | `/doctor:mcp install` | the checkout | Builds and registers Code Mode, the bridge your runtime uses to call MCP tools |\n150: | 4 | `/doctor:git setup` | your project | Checks the git hooks and sk-git settings. Run `/doctor:git standards` afterwards to write repo-owned commit, PR and branch rules; until then the shipped defaults apply |\n151: | 5 | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | your project | Sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server |\n152: | 6 | `/doctor:setup` | your project | Confirms the whole setup works |\n153: \n154: If you chose `link` for the instruction file, step 1 also carries `--link-instructions` and step 2 drops out.\n155: \n156: ### Step 3: Check the Links\n157: \n158: ```\n159: /doctor:symlink check --root <dir>\n160: ```\n161: \n162: Each folder should read `linked-whole` or `linked-merge`. A folder that reads `partial-merge` lacks entries the checkout gained since your last `link`. Run `link` again to add them.\n163: \n164: ### What Gets Linked\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 165]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file INSTALL-SKILLED.md, lines 120-164\n120: ## 3. LINK IT INTO YOUR PROJECT\n121: \n122: ### Step 1: Run the Install Guide\n123: \n124: Open your Skilled checkout in your runtime and run:\n125: \n126: ```\n127: /doctor:install\n128: ```\n129: \n130: It asks four questions in one prompt:\n131: \n132: 1. **Target repo:** the absolute path of your project.\n133: 2. **Runtimes:** the AI coding tools you use. Pick any of `claude`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin` and `pi`.\n134: 3. **Link shape:** choose `auto`. [What Gets Linked](#what-gets-linked) explains the shapes.\n135: 4. **Instruction file:** `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md` and leaves a one-line `CLAUDE.md` reading `@AGENTS.md`, because Claude Code reads only `CLAUDE.md`. `link` points `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` at the checkout's copies.\n136: \n137: <!-- readme-check\n138: allow-ref CLAUDE.md | the instruction file in the operator's target repo, which this checkout does not ship\n139: -->\n140: \n141: The guide writes nothing. It prints the steps below with your paths filled in.\n142: \n143: ### Step 2: Run the Printed Steps\n144: \n145: | Step | Command | Run it from | What it does |\n146: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n147: | 1 | `/doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode auto` | the checkout | Links `.skilled` and your runtime folders into the project |\n148: | 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md` and leaves the CLAUDE.md pointer. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n149: | 3 | `/doctor:mcp install` | the checkout | Builds and registers Code Mode, the bridge your runtime uses to call MCP tools |\n150: | 4 | `/doctor:git setup` | your project | Checks the git hooks and sk-git settings. Run `/doctor:git standards` afterwards to write repo-owned commit, PR and branch rules; until then the shipped defaults apply |\n151: | 5 | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | your project | Sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server |\n152: | 6 | `/doctor:setup` | your project | Confirms the whole setup works |\n153: \n154: If you chose `link` for the instruction file, step 1 also carries `--link-instructions` and step 2 drops out.\n155: \n156: ### Step 3: Check the Links\n157: \n158: ```\n159: /doctor:symlink check --root <dir>\n160: ```\n161: \n162: Each folder should read `linked-whole` or `linked-merge`. A folder that reads `partial-merge` lacks entries the checkout gained since your last `link`. Run `link` again to add them.\n163: \n164: ### What Gets Linked\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 165]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"l