rinted. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:48:+-- hook-wiring-check.cjs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:112:| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | The read-only hook-wiring check: it reads `.claude/settings.json`, `.codex/hooks.json`, `.cursor/hooks.json` and `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, and reports whether the prompt hook entry is present for each runtime folder it finds. `--root <dir>` is required and `--json` prints one object. It prints `ok <runtime>` or `hook-missing <runtime> <file>`, skips a runtime whose folder is absent and never writes. It exits 0 when every installed runtime is wired, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:235:| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It writes no file and runs no installer, and its JSON form reports the same readings as its lines. It exits 0 when every installed runtime carries its entry, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:40:  hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:61:    - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37:  hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60:    - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:48:+-- hook-wiring-check.cjs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:112:| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | The read-only hook-wiring check: it reads `.claude/settings.json`, `.codex/hooks.json`, `.cursor/hooks.json` and `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, and reports whether the prompt hook entry is present for each runtime folder it finds. `--root <dir>` is required and `--json` prints one object. It prints `ok <runtime>` or `hook-missing <runtime> <file>`, skips a runtime whose folder is absent and never writes. It exits 0 when every installed runtime is wired, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:235:| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It writes no file and runs no installer, and its JSON form reports the same readings as its lines. It exits 0 when every installed runtime carries its entry, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -rn \\\"hook-wiring-check\\\\|JSON.stringify\\\\|payload\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570721305,"end":1794570722006}}}}
