{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794570725915,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"id":"prt_1d4c02a1b0017kaRYra6CSkSi9","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4c02116001yFuiCQXeJ74Hnj","type":"step-start","snapshot":"f0f67d8a3569c706c7d3a3779c0796721d0fd625"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570750086,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c0874600183n71ZbJmlmWV8","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4c02116001yFuiCQXeJ74Hnj","type":"tool","id":"call_4a51a61b04e04ce2b751106d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '240,300p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt"},"output":"Re-read: [the check engine's result line]\nSTATUS=OK\n```\n\n### Failure Summary\n\n```text\nDOCTOR TARGET FAILED\nTarget: [check|embed|restore]\nStep: [the phase or row that stopped the run]\nError: [the engine's code and message]\nChanged: [what was written before the failure, or none]\nNext: [the repair, or the accepted invocation]\nSTATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[code]\"\n```\n\nA check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"`. An embed that exits 1 after its proof found a dropped line restored from the backup by itself, so its `Changed:` is `none` and its `Next:` names the file whose line went missing. An embed that exits 3 had a write fail after its backup. Its Changed: is none when the output holds restored:, and otherwise the reply says the tree is partly written and its Next: is the undo command the engine printed.\n\n## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n\n| Situation | Suggested Action |\n|-----------|------------------|\n| A check row reports `FINDING` | Read that row's detail, fix that one requirement, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` |\n| A check row reports `UNKNOWN` | The row could not be answered, not failed. Rerun when its precondition is back, and never report an `UNKNOWN` row as a pass |\n| `A1` reports `stale`, `forked` or `foreign` | `/doctor:agents-md embed` shows what the run would compose and what it would carry before anything is written |\n| `A8` or `A9` reports content | The lines are the repository's own. An embed carries them into the block. A line that must stay routed belongs in a rule file authored through the create-repo-rule route |\n| `A6` reports a budget finding | The composed document is past the byte ceiling a truncating runtime stops at. Every carried line is still kept, and the finding is the operator's to resolve |\n| `A11` reports missing router rows | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds the shipped rows that are missing and touches no other row |\n| `A10` reports a runtime copy out of sync, or the apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | The generator rewrites an existing `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` and never creates a missing one, so a missing file stays missing however often the embed reruns. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` lists the generated runtime mirrors that drift, each with the write form of the checker that owns it; the pointer block is not one of the files that route checks, so a `missing` line on it means the file has to exist first. Create `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --root <root>`, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` and read `A10` again |\n| The embed question was answered no | Nothing was written. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` when the plan is acceptable |\n| The apply reports a digest that does not match | The tree changed after the plan. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` so the plan and the digest describe the tree in front of you |\n| The apply reports a dropped line | The engine restored from the backup by itself. Read the dropped line, keep it in the block or in a reference document, then rerun the plan |\n| The embed is not wanted after all | `/doctor:agents-md restore --run=<the backup folder the apply printed>` puts back the files that run wrote |\n| A restore reports a hash that does not match | The record or one of its copies changed, so nothing was written. Read the message. The backup at that directory is kept |\n| A restore reports that the record names another root | The record belongs to the folder it names, and nothing was written. Rerun the restore with `--root <the root the record names>`, in the spaced form: `--root=` is not accepted |\n| Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n\n## 8. Next Step\n\n| Condition | Suggested Command | Reason |\n|-----------|-------------------|--------|\n| A check row still reports `FINDING` after an embed | `/doctor:agents-md check` | The write is complete, and the remaining row is a different requirement |\n| The composed document is past the byte ceiling | `/doctor:agents-md check` | A6 names the ceiling and what the run kept anyway |\n| The repository has no `REPO RULES.md` | `/doctor:agents-md embed --create-router` | The router is created from the shipped rows and the checker runs after it |\n| The apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | It lists each generated runtime mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker, and `A10` names the copy that is still unverified |\n| A rule belongs in a routed file rather than the always-on block | `/create:repo-rule` | Action-triggered rules belong in a rule file that `REPO RULES.md` routes, not in a document every agent loads |\n| A release unit or a `.skilled/**` path needs changing | `/doctor:update` | This command owns the root instruction files, and the release tree belongs to the updater |\n\nEnd interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Re-read: [the check engine's result line]\nSTATUS=OK\n```\n\n### Failure Summary\n\n```text\nDOCTOR TARGET FAILED\nTarget: [check|embed|restore]\nStep: [the phase or row that stopped the run]\nError: [the engine's code and message]\nChanged: [what was written before the failure, or none]\nNext: [the repair, or the accepted invocation]\nSTATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[code]\"\n```\n\nA check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"`. An embed that exits 1 after its proof found a dropped line restored from the backup by itself, so its `Changed:` is `none` and its `Next:` names the file whose line went missing. An embed that exits 3 had a write fail after its backup. Its Changed: is none when the output holds restored:, and otherwise the reply says the tree is partly written and its Next: is the undo command the engine printed.\n\n## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n\n| Situation | Suggested Action |\n|-----------|------------------|\n| A check row reports `FINDING` | Read that row's detail, fix that one requirement, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` |\n| A check row reports `UNKNOWN` | The row could not be answered, not failed. Rerun when its precondition is back, and never report an `UNKNOWN` row as a pass |\n| `A1` reports `stale`, `forked` or `foreign` | `/doctor:agents-md embed` shows what the run would compose and what it would carry before anything is written |\n| `A8` or `A9` reports content | The lines are the repository's own. An embed carries them into the block. A line that must stay routed belongs in a rule file authored through the create-repo-rule route |\n| `A6` reports a budget finding | The composed document is past the byte ceiling a truncating runtime stops at. Every carried line is still kept, and the finding is the operator's to resolve |\n| `A11` reports missing router rows | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds the shipped rows that are missing and touches no other row |\n| `A10` reports a runtime copy out of sync, or the apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | The generator rewrites an existing `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` and never creates a missing one, so a missing file stays missing however often the embed reruns. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` lists the generated runtime mirrors that drift, each with the write form of the checker that owns it; the pointer block is not one of the files that route checks, so a `missing` line on it means the file has to exist first. Create `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --root <root>`, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` and read `A10` again |\n| The embed question was answered no | Nothing was written. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` when the plan is acceptable |\n| The apply reports a digest that does not match | The tree changed after the plan. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` so the plan and the digest describe the tree in front of you |\n| The apply reports a dropped line | The engine restored from the backup by itself. Read the dropped line, keep it in the block or in a reference document, then rerun the plan |\n| The embed is not wanted after all | `/doctor:agents-md restore --run=<the backup folder the apply printed>` puts back the files that run wrote |\n| A restore reports a hash that does not match | The record or one of its copies changed, so nothing was written. Read the message. The backup at that directory is kept |\n| A restore reports that the record names another root | The record belongs to the folder it names, and nothing was written. Rerun the restore with `--root <the root the record names>`, in the spaced form: `--root=` is not accepted |\n| Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n\n## 8. Next Step\n\n| Condition | Suggested Command | Reason |\n|-----------|-------------------|--------|\n| A check row still reports `FINDING` after an embed | `/doctor:agents-md check` | The write is complete, and the remaining row is a different requirement |\n| The composed document is past the byte ceiling | `/doctor:agents-md check` | A6 names the ceiling and what the run kept anyway |\n| The repository has no `REPO RULES.md` | `/doctor:agents-md embed --create-router` | The router is created from the shipped rows and the checker runs after it |\n| The apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | It lists each generated runtime mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker, and `A10` names the copy that is still unverified |\n| A rule belongs in a routed file rather than the always-on block | `/create:repo-rule` | Action-triggered rules belong in a rule file that `REPO RULES.md` routes, not in a document every agent loads |\n| A release unit or a `.skilled/**` path needs changing | `/doctor:update` | This command owns the root instruction files, and the release tree belongs to the updater |\n\nEnd interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '240,300p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570749766,"end":1794570750086}}}}
