{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570910942,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c2faac002bzPiVzCZ5R98bI","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4c2eadd001bA6Ry6lWQz2UWU","type":"tool","id":"call_7b7f11a485ea43379eb22ccc","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"Ollama\\|ollama\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md | head -40"},"output":"277:The skill-advisor `semantic_shadow` lane runs against a pluggable embedder layer. As of phase `003/006` the contract surface (adapter interface, types, manifest registry, Ollama adapter) lives in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor now owns. Skill-advisor's local `runtime/lib/embedders/` files are thin re-export shims plus a skill-advisor-specific `schema.ts` integration that targets the package-local SQLite database at `runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite`. This section is the new-user onboarding view; the canonical embedder narrative lives at [embedder-pluggability.md](../system-spec-kit/references/memory/embedder-pluggability.md).\n285:| 1 | Ollama running with a known text manifest pulled | `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` (first match in priority list) |\n298:| Name | Dim | Backend | Ollama tag | Max input | Notes |\n300:| `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` | 768 | `ollama` | `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 5000 | 768-dim retrieval specialist. Local-first cascade default per ADR-014. Uses `search_query: ` / `search_document: ` prefix tokens. |\n301:| `mxbai-embed-large-v1` | 1024 | `ollama` | `mxbai-embed-large:latest` | 1200 | Phase `016/004` paraphrase-strong candidate. |\n302:| `bge-small-en-v1.5` | 384 | `ollama` | `bge-small-en-v1.5:latest` | n/a | Compact 33M-param baseline. |\n303:| `bge-large-en-v1.5` | 1024 | `ollama` | `bge-large-en-v1.5:latest` | n/a | BAAI flagship retrieval model. |\n304:| `jina-embeddings-v3` | 1024 | `ollama` | `hf.co/gaianet/jina-embeddings-v3-GGUF:Q4_K_M` | 8000 | Multilingual + paraphrase-tuned. Matryoshka representation allows 256 / 512 / 768 / 1024 truncation. |\n305:| `bge-m3` | 1024 | `ollama` | `bge-m3:latest` | 8000 | Multilingual hybrid (dense + sparse + colbert). |\n306:| `snowflake-arctic-embed-l-v2.0` | 1024 | `ollama` | `snowflake-arctic-embed2:latest` | 8000 | Snowflake late-2024 flagship. 8192 context, multilingual, top MTEB retrieval scores. |\n356:| `ollama` (default after cascade picks tier 1) | Ollama owns runtime device handling. It already covers Metal / CUDA / CPU autonomously based on its own daemon configuration. |\n360:If you need MPS-style auto-detect for a local model, the Ollama backend already provides it on Apple Silicon by default — install Ollama, pull a manifest, the cascade picks it.\n365:- Shared contract surface: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/) — the canonical adapter, types, registry and Ollama adapter.\n366:- Shared cascade: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts) — file-locked Ollama → hf-local → OpenAI → Voyage probe chain (ADR-014 local-first). Accepts optional `contentType: 'text' \\| 'code'` parameter (default `'text'`).\n372:`/doctor:install` includes the embedder setup by default, and the setup itself runs as `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` from inside the target repo. The route probes `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true`, prints one plan row per missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks once before it runs anything. A no stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` and changes nothing. `--dry-run` prints the plan and stops with `STATUS=OK`. The route never installs or upgrades Ollama: it prints the install command for the operator, and the install guide owns that cost. The two health flags split the diagnosis: `includeEmbeddingsHealth` probes only the hf-local model server, while `includeSemanticHealth` reports the active embedder and probes its backend.\n379:| Idle memory, `ollama serve` with no model loaded | 25776 KB (25.2 MiB) |\n381:| Unload after the last call | 5 minutes, Ollama keep-alive |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"277:The skill-advisor `semantic_shadow` lane runs against a pluggable embedder layer. As of phase `003/006` the contract surface (adapter interface, types, manifest registry, Ollama adapter) lives in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor now owns. Skill-advisor's local `runtime/lib/embedders/` files are thin re-export shims plus a skill-advisor-specific `schema.ts` integration that targets the package-local SQLite database at `runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite`. This section is the new-user onboarding view; the canonical embedder narrative lives at [embedder-pluggability.md](../system-spec-kit/references/memory/embedder-pluggability.md).\n285:| 1 | Ollama running with a known text manifest pulled | `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` (first match in priority list) |\n298:| Name | Dim | Backend | Ollama tag | Max input | Notes |\n300:| `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` | 768 | `ollama` | `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 5000 | 768-dim retrieval specialist. Local-first cascade default per ADR-014. Uses `search_query: ` / `search_document: ` prefix tokens. |\n301:| `mxbai-embed-large-v1` | 1024 | `ollama` | `mxbai-embed-large:latest` | 1200 | Phase `016/004` paraphrase-strong candidate. |\n302:| `bge-small-en-v1.5` | 384 | `ollama` | `bge-small-en-v1.5:latest` | n/a | Compact 33M-param baseline. |\n303:| `bge-large-en-v1.5` | 1024 | `ollama` | `bge-large-en-v1.5:latest` | n/a | BAAI flagship retrieval model. |\n304:| `jina-embeddings-v3` | 1024 | `ollama` | `hf.co/gaianet/jina-embeddings-v3-GGUF:Q4_K_M` | 8000 | Multilingual + paraphrase-tuned. Matryoshka representation allows 256 / 512 / 768 / 1024 truncation. |\n305:| `bge-m3` | 1024 | `ollama` | `bge-m3:latest` | 8000 | Multilingual hybrid (dense + sparse + colbert). |\n306:| `snowflake-arctic-embed-l-v2.0` | 1024 | `ollama` | `snowflake-arctic-embed2:latest` | 8000 | Snowflake late-2024 flagship. 8192 context, multilingual, top MTEB retrieval scores. |\n356:| `ollama` (default after cascade picks tier 1) | Ollama owns runtime device handling. It already covers Metal / CUDA / CPU autonomously based on its own daemon configuration. |\n360:If you need MPS-style auto-detect for a local model, the Ollama backend already provides it on Apple Silicon by default — install Ollama, pull a manifest, the cascade picks it.\n365:- Shared contract surface: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/) — the canonical adapter, types, registry and Ollama adapter.\n366:- Shared cascade: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts) — file-locked Ollama → hf-local → OpenAI → Voyage probe chain (ADR-014 local-first). Accepts optional `contentType: 'text' \\| 'code'` parameter (default `'text'`).\n372:`/doctor:install` includes the embedder setup by default, and the setup itself runs as `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` from inside the target repo. The route probes `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true`, prints one plan row per missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks once before it runs anything. A no stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` and changes nothing. `--dry-run` prints the plan and stops with `STATUS=OK`. The route never installs or upgrades Ollama: it prints the install command for the operator, and the install guide owns that cost. The two health flags split the diagnosis: `includeEmbeddingsHealth` probes only the hf-local model server, while `includeSemanticHealth` reports the active embedder and probes its backend.\n379:| Idle memory, `ollama serve` with no model loaded | 25776 KB (25.2 MiB) |\n381:| Unload after the last call | 5 minutes, Ollama keep-alive |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"Ollama\\\\|ollama\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570910380,"end":1794570910942}}}}
