{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794570915394,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"id":"prt_1d4c30e42001PoRepYgxEtjHtf","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4c30439001KO09dLUEdHhnqS","type":"step-start","snapshot":"7091b37e336128ccf71f6f630dab2fed18f061d7"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570917383,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c3147b002i11gf3wzdpXjWY","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4c30439001KO09dLUEdHhnqS","type":"tool","id":"call_25e37178cf80431e80a6f7ff","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":30,"offset":366,"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md, lines 366-395\n366: - Shared cascade: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts) — file-locked Ollama → hf-local → OpenAI → Voyage probe chain (ADR-014 local-first). Accepts optional `contentType: 'text' \\| 'code'` parameter (default `'text'`).\n367: - Skill-advisor schema helpers: [`runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts`](./runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts).\n368: - Architecture-gap follow-on: packet `003/006-shared-embedder-logic-with-spec-memory` (shipped phase 003/006).\n369: \n370: ### 12.7 Setup route and cost\n371: \n372: `/doctor:install` includes the embedder setup by default, and the setup itself runs as `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` from inside the target repo. The route probes `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true`, prints one plan row per missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks once before it runs anything. A no stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` and changes nothing. `--dry-run` prints the plan and stops with `STATUS=OK`. The route never installs or upgrades Ollama: it prints the install command for the operator, and the install guide owns that cost. The two health flags split the diagnosis: `includeEmbeddingsHealth` probes only the hf-local model server, while `includeSemanticHealth` reports the active embedder and probes its backend.\n373: \n374: What the embedder costs on this machine, measured 2026-11-13 with `runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`:\n375: \n376: | Measure | Value |\n377: | --- | ---: |\n378: | Disk for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 274302450 bytes (261.6 MiB) |\n379: | Idle memory, `ollama serve` with no model loaded | 25776 KB (25.2 MiB) |\n380: | Loaded memory, model runner resident | 279520 KB (273.0 MiB) |\n381: | Unload after the last call | 5 minutes, Ollama keep-alive |\n382: | Warm embed latency, model loaded | 4.8 ms median, 8.9 ms p95 |\n383: | Cold first call after the unload | 538.53 ms |\n384: \n385: Once the approved steps ran, the route runs `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`. That scan is what writes the command vectors into the `vec_cmd_<dim>` table: without it `commandVectorCoverage.embedded` stays at zero and the semantic lane reports off. The database is derived state and gitignored, since `.gitignore` ignores `runtime/database/*.sqlite`, so the scan costs its own runtime plus the warm latency per embedded prompt and leaves nothing for git.\n386: \n387: ---\n388: \n389: ## 13. RELATED RESOURCES\n390: \n391: | Document | Purpose |\n392: | --- | --- |\n393: | [README.md](./README.md) | Operator overview, quick start, runtime integrations. |\n394: | [ARCHITECTURE.md](./ARCHITECTURE.md) | Package-local architecture and public API entrypoints. |\n395: | [Hook reference](./hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md) | Prompt-time hook surfaces for each runtime. |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 396]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md, lines 366-395\n366: - Shared cascade: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts) — file-locked Ollama → hf-local → OpenAI → Voyage probe chain (ADR-014 local-first). Accepts optional `contentType: 'text' \\| 'code'` parameter (default `'text'`).\n367: - Skill-advisor schema helpers: [`runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts`](./runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts).\n368: - Architecture-gap follow-on: packet `003/006-shared-embedder-logic-with-spec-memory` (shipped phase 003/006).\n369: \n370: ### 12.7 Setup route and cost\n371: \n372: `/doctor:install` includes the embedder setup by default, and the setup itself runs as `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` from inside the target repo. The route probes `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true`, prints one plan row per missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks once before it runs anything. A no stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` and changes nothing. `--dry-run` prints the plan and stops with `STATUS=OK`. The route never installs or upgrades Ollama: it prints the install command for the operator, and the install guide owns that cost. The two health flags split the diagnosis: `includeEmbeddingsHealth` probes only the hf-local model server, while `includeSemanticHealth` reports the active embedder and probes its backend.\n373: \n374: What the embedder costs on this machine, measured 2026-11-13 with `runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`:\n375: \n376: | Measure | Value |\n377: | --- | ---: |\n378: | Disk for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 274302450 bytes (261.6 MiB) |\n379: | Idle memory, `ollama serve` with no model loaded | 25776 KB (25.2 MiB) |\n380: | Loaded memory, model runner resident | 279520 KB (273.0 MiB) |\n381: | Unload after the last call | 5 minutes, Ollama keep-alive |\n382: | Warm embed latency, model loaded | 4.8 ms median, 8.9 ms p95 |\n383: | Cold first call after the unload | 538.53 ms |\n384: \n385: Once the approved steps ran, the route runs `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`. That scan is what writes the command vectors into the `vec_cmd_<dim>` table: without it `commandVectorCoverage.embedded` stays at zero and the semantic lane reports off. The database is derived state and gitignored, since `.gitignore` ignores `runtime/database/*.sqlite`, so the scan costs its own runtime plus the warm latency per embedded prompt and leaves nothing for git.\n386: \n387: ---\n388: \n389: ## 13. RELATED RESOURCES\n390: \n391: | Document | Purpose |\n392: | --- | --- |\n393: | [README.md](./README.md) | Operator overview, quick start, runtime integrations. |\n394: | [ARCHITECTURE.md](./ARCHITECTURE.md) | Package-local architecture and public API entrypoints. |\n395: | [Hook reference](./hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md) | Prompt-time hook surfaces for each runtime. |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 396]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":30,\"offset\":366,\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570916987,"end":1794570917383}}}}
