{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571018955,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c49e5a0010hoI1TGXkzhKBZ","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4c4803d001l5w1M56lqfqIpz","type":"tool","id":"call_1c3c0c5c95994c02864eba02","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls .dsh 2>/dev/null; find .dsh -maxdepth 3 -type f 2>/dev/null | head -20; grep -rn \"prompt-advisor\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime 2>/dev/null | head -10"},"output":"agents\nmanual-testing-playbook\npatches\nplugins\nprompts\nREADME.md\nskills\nSYNC.md\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/lineage-leaf.mjs\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs\n.dsh/patches/mcp-code-mode.patch.yml\n.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml\n.dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml\n.dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml\n.dsh/patches/lineage.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/deep-review.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/deep-research.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/prompt-improver.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/debug.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/markdown.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/review.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/code.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/orchestrate.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/design.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/context.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/ai-council.patch.yml\n.dsh/README.md\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/tests/dsh-prompt-advisor.test.mjs:13:import { ADVISOR_RUNTIME, ERROR_POLICY as advisorPolicy, registerPromptAdvisor, runAdvisor } from '../dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs';\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs:96:    ctx.logger.warn(`repo-guards prompt-advisor: ${String(error)}`);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/README.md:16:`hooks/dsh/` holds the real file behind the `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` link. Node resolves the link to this path before it resolves the file's imports, so its relative imports are written for this folder. The index link `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` points back here.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/README.md:22:`prompt-advisor.mjs` runs on `agent/pre-step` and proxies the latest prompt the operator typed through the compiled Claude `user-prompt-submit.js` chain into this skill's advisor. Guard notices and runtime-context snapshots are user-role messages too, so only a message whose source is `user` counts as the prompt. The adapter passes the runtime label `dsh`, which the advisor's runtime list in `runtime/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts` accepts, so its metrics and outcome records carry the right runtime. The brief comes back as `additionalContext` and joins the step as one notice. It fails open.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/README.md:16:`hooks/pi/` holds the real file behind the `.pi/extensions/prompt-advisor.ts` entry file. Pi discovers it through that one-line entry file, which re-exports it, so it loads from this folder. `ADVISOR_HOOK_FALLBACK_MODULE` is the folder-relative specifier that resolves there. `ADVISOR_HOOK_MODULE` is the long form left from the link-based layout. It is tried first and does not resolve from this folder, so under Pi the fallback is the one that loads. One test resolves the long form against `.pi/extensions/prompt-advisor.ts`, where it still points at the compiled hook.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/README.md:22:`prompt-advisor.ts` fires on Pi's `input` event and proxies the turn through the compiled Claude `user-prompt-submit.js` chain into this skill's advisor. The call passes `runtime: 'pi'`, so advisor diagnostics carry `pi`. It races a timer of the advisor budget (`SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS`, default 2500 ms) plus 300 ms and delivers the fallback directive if the call hangs past it. Debug output labels a fallback `fallback(outage)`, `fallback(no-match)`, `fallback(skipped)` or `fallback(headless)`. The advisor's brief, `Advisor: <freshness>; use <skill> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` plus the fixed comment-hygiene directive, comes back as `additionalContext` and is appended to the user's own prompt text via Pi's input-transform, making it **operator-visible in Pi's chat** (every other runtime injects it invisibly). Transforms chain additively with the spec-gate classifier on the same event. Fails open.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:92:| **Pi** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` (real file, re-exported by its one-line `.pi/extensions/` entry) | `user_input` / prompt event via `.pi/extensions/` | Imports the advisor module **in-process** (not a subprocess). Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send. In-process calls remove the stall and let the module-level prompt cache work. Captures raw user text (bounded 32 KiB, 64-session LRU). The in-process call passes `runtime: 'pi'` and races a timer of the advisor budget plus 300 ms, delivering the fallback directives if the call hangs | Model-visible message. Delivery-state machine suppresses same-session re-delivery |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:94:| **DSH** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` | `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false` | Proxies the latest operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `dsh`. A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief | Brief added to the step |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:126:|   `-- prompt-advisor.mjs            # real DSH adapter (.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ imports it)\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:129:|   `-- prompt-advisor.ts             # real Pi extension (.pi/extensions/ re-exports it)\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"agents\nmanual-testing-playbook\npatches\nplugins\nprompts\nREADME.md\nskills\nSYNC.md\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/lineage-leaf.mjs\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs\n.dsh/patches/mcp-code-mode.patch.yml\n.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml\n.dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml\n.dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml\n.dsh/patches/lineage.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/deep-review.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/deep-research.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/prompt-improver.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/debug.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/markdown.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/review.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/code.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/orchestrate.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/design.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/context.patch.yml\n.dsh/agents/ai-council.patch.yml\n.dsh/README.md\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/tests/dsh-prompt-advisor.test.mjs:13:import { ADVISOR_RUNTIME, ERROR_POLICY as advisorPolicy, registerPromptAdvisor, runAdvisor } from '../dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs';\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs:96:    ctx.logger.warn(`repo-guards prompt-advisor: ${String(error)}`);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/README.md:16:`hooks/dsh/` holds the real file behind the `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` link. Node resolves the link to this path before it resolves the file's imports, so its relative imports are written for this folder. The index link `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` points back here.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/README.md:22:`prompt-advisor.mjs` runs on `agent/pre-step` and proxies the latest prompt the operator typed through the compiled Claude `user-prompt-submit.js` chain into this skill's advisor. Guard notices and runtime-context snapshots are user-role messages too, so only a message whose source is `user` counts as the prompt. The adapter passes the runtime label `dsh`, which the advisor's runtime list in `runtime/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts` accepts, so its metrics and outcome records carry the right runtime. The brief comes back as `additionalContext` and joins the step as one notice. It fails open.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/README.md:16:`hooks/pi/` holds the real file behind the `.pi/extensions/prompt-advisor.ts` entry file. Pi discovers it through that one-line entry file, which re-exports it, so it loads from this folder. `ADVISOR_HOOK_FALLBACK_MODULE` is the folder-relative specifier that resolves there. `ADVISOR_HOOK_MODULE` is the long form left from the link-based layout. It is tried first and does not resolve from this folder, so under Pi the fallback is the one that loads. One test resolves the long form against `.pi/extensions/prompt-advisor.ts`, where it still points at the compiled hook.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/README.md:22:`prompt-advisor.ts` fires on Pi's `input` event and proxies the turn through the compiled Claude `user-prompt-submit.js` chain into this skill's advisor. The call passes `runtime: 'pi'`, so advisor diagnostics carry `pi`. It races a timer of the advisor budget (`SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS`, default 2500 ms) plus 300 ms and delivers the fallback directive if the call hangs past it. Debug output labels a fallback `fallback(outage)`, `fallback(no-match)`, `fallback(skipped)` or `fallback(headless)`. The advisor's brief, `Advisor: <freshness>; use <skill> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` plus the fixed comment-hygiene directive, comes back as `additionalContext` and is appended to the user's own prompt text via Pi's input-transform, making it **operator-visible in Pi's chat** (every other runtime injects it invisibly). Transforms chain additively with the spec-gate classifier on the same event. Fails open.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:92:| **Pi** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` (real file, re-exported by its one-line `.pi/extensions/` entry) | `user_input` / prompt event via `.pi/extensions/` | Imports the advisor module **in-process** (not a subprocess). Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send. In-process calls remove the stall and let the module-level prompt cache work. Captures raw user text (bounded 32 KiB, 64-session LRU). The in-process call passes `runtime: 'pi'` and races a timer of the advisor budget plus 300 ms, delivering the fallback directives if the call hangs | Model-visible message. Delivery-state machine suppresses same-session re-delivery |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:94:| **DSH** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` | `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false` | Proxies the latest operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `dsh`. A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief | Brief added to the step |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:126:|   `-- prompt-advisor.mjs            # real DSH adapter (.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ imports it)\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:129:|   `-- prompt-advisor.ts             # real Pi extension (.pi/extensions/ re-exports it)\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"ls .dsh 2>/dev/null; find .dsh -maxdepth 3 -type f 2>/dev/null | head -20; grep -rn \\\"prompt-advisor\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime 2>/dev/null | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571017818,"end":1794571018955}}}}
