\\\"findingsBySeverity\\\": {\\n    \\\"P0\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"P1\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"P2\\\": 0\\n  },\\n  \\\"openFindingsCount\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"resolvedFindingsCount\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"convergenceScore\\\": 0.0\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571150640,"end":1794571171592}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571171596,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c6aa58001FmdGbJPZ0BEybs","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4c699bc001x3wByKmwWpjIQ8","type":"tool","id":"call_fd5dfdce1f16435ea612bf9c","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Deep Review Strategy - Doctor Install Pass Two\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder), area `doctor-install`.\n- Purpose: verify every pass-one doctor-install fix holds, review every file changed since pass one line by line, then look for new defects.\n- Mutability: updated by the orchestrator and by each iteration; reducer-owned counts are refreshed after every iteration.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nReview: command surfacing pass two, doctor-install lineage. Scope is the doctor install, setup, symlink, runtime-mirrors and AGENTS.md routes plus the scripts and tests they own.\n\n---\n\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Re-report a pass-one finding whose fix holds, a deferred item from report section 8, R4-P2-003, or the refuted finding.\n- Review any file outside the 30 doctor-install area paths.\n- Read or print holdout prompt text. The doctor-install area opens no holdout file.\n- Change code. This lineage writes only its own review packet.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Composite convergence score at or above 0.60 with all four dimensions covered, or seven iterations.\n- A P0 or P1 finding keeps the verdict at FAIL or CONDITIONAL; it never blocks recording the iteration.\n\n---\n\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n| [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n\n[Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading the remediation diff first, then the surrounding function, kept every pass-one verdict tied to the current bytes (iteration 1).\n- Running the changed `node --test` files gave a whole-gate baseline before any finding was recorded (iterations 1 to 4).\n- Probing `hook-wiring-check.cjs` with temporary hook fixtures exposed wrapper shapes the unit tests do not cover (iteration 3).\n- Comparing the setup leg's hook-health claim against `metrics.ts` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` found a surviving pass-one doc defect (iteration 4).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- The pass-one fix for the setup absent-hook-health message names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` as the switch that turns records on; the writer records every prompt by default and the flag only adds two fields (iteration 4).\n- The new exit-3 contract covers `restored:` and `nothing was restored` but not the engine's `the restore failed` path (iteration 1).\n- The narrowed hook-wiring matcher does not recognise `env node ...` or `bash -lc \"node ...\"` wrappers (iteration 3).\n\n---\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n### Pass-one fix verification -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration 1)\n- What worked: reading the remediation diff beside the pass-one one-line fix, then running the owning test file.\n- Prefer for: every remaining pass-one finding in this area.\n\n### String-containment marker scan -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, one attempt)\n- What was tried: keeping the old `JSON.stringify(payload).includes(marker)` check.\n- Why blocked: it passes a description-only mention, which is the pass-one DR5-P2-002 defect.\n- Do NOT retry: match the serialized payload; walk `type: command` entries instead.\n\n---\n\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n- The pass-one DR1-P1-001 write-failure fix is incomplete -- ruled out: the engine restores, prints backup and undo, and exits 3; the remaining gap is the route text for a second restore fault (iteration 1, evidence: `agents-md-embed.cjs:1425-1439`).\n- The pass-one DR4-P1-001 symlink fix misses the link-install mode -- ruled out: `compose` refuses the router and mirror when the action would write, and `assertWritable` refuses a link that resolves outside the root (iteration 1, evidence: `agents-md-embed.cjs:819-829`).\n- A malformed router row still reads as missing -- ruled out: `parseTableRows` keeps the row and A11 prints its line and width (iteration 2, evidence: `agents-md-check.cjs:803-826`).\n- The pass-one Q3 fix is complete -- not ruled out: the setup YAML names the absent state, but `setup.md:82` names the wrong switch (iteration 4, evidence: `metrics.ts:451-464`).\n\n---\n\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Focus area: the four pass-one embed-engine fixes and the changed embed tests\n- Reason: the engine is the only mutating surface in this area and its exit contract changed\n- Required evidence: direct read of the changed ranges plus the owning test file\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n- The pass-one report (`review/review-report-pass-1.md`) lists 43 merged findings; 17 belong to this area, all P2 after verification.\n- The remediation range is `320e7b64d4..HEAD` (HEAD `087888ec4a`); 21 doctor-install files changed.\n- The pass-one lineage (`review/lineages/doctor-install/`) stopped at its five-iteration cap with a last novelty ratio of 0.125, so this pass exists to verify the fixes and converge.\n- The doctor-install area touches four prompt-hook runtimes (claude, codex, cursor, devin); opencode, pi and dsh have no advisor hook entry in this checkout, and `hook-wiring-check.cjs` skips them by design.\n- Holdout files belong to the accuracy-runner area. This lineage opened none and reports counts only where a doc mentions them.\n\n---\n\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | Packet docs read in iteration 4 |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | No checklist row claimed yet |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | - | No skill or agent definition in this area |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | Runtime coverage read in iteration 3 |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | Feature catalog describes the advisor, not the doctor routes |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | - | No playbook file in this area |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| [path/to/file] | [D1, D3] | [N] | [0 P0, 1 P1, 2 P2] | [partial/complete] |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Max iterations: 7\n- Convergence threshold: 0.10\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-doctor-install-2-1794570021136-noekp0, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Severity threshold: P2\n- Review target type: spec-folder\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n- Started: 2026-11-13T12:40:00.000Z\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Deep Review Strategy - Doctor Install Pass Two\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder), area `doctor-install`.\\n- Purpose: verify every pass-one doctor-install fix holds, review every file changed since pass one line by line, then look for new defects.\\n- Mutability: updated by the orchestrator and by each iteration; reducer-owned counts are refreshed after every iteration.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nReview: command surfacing pass two, doctor-install lineage. Scope is the doctor install, setup, symlink, runtime-mirrors and AGENTS.md routes plus the scripts and tests they own.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Re-report a pass-one finding whose fix holds, a deferred item from report section 8, R4-P2-003, or the refuted finding.\\n- Review any file outside the 30 doctor-install area paths.\\n- Read or print holdout prompt text. The doctor-install area opens no holdout file.\\n- Change code. This lineage writes only its own review packet.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Composite convergence score at or above 0.60 with all four dimensions covered, or seven iterations.\\n- A P0 or P1 finding keeps the verdict at FAIL or CONDITIONAL; it never blocks recording the iteration.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\\n\\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\\n| [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\\n\\n[Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Reading the remediation diff first, then the surrounding function, kept every pass-one verdict tied to the current bytes (iteration 1).\\n- Running the changed `node --test` files gave a whole-gate baseline before any finding was recorded (iterations 1 to 4).\\n- Probing `hook-wiring-check.cjs` with temporary hook fixtures exposed wrapper shapes the unit tests do not cover (iteration 3).\\n- Comparing the setup leg's hook-health claim against `metrics.ts` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` found a surviving pass-one doc defect (iteration 4).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- The pass-one fix for the setup absent-hook-health message names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` as the switch that turns records on; the writer records every prompt by default and the flag only adds two fields (iteration 4).\\n- The new exit-3 contract covers `restored:` and `nothing was restored` but not the engine's `the restore failed` path (iteration 1).\\n- The narrowed hook-wiring matcher does not recognise `env node ...` or `bash -lc \\\"node ...\\\"` wrappers (iteration 3).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\n### Pass-one fix verification -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration 1)\\n- What worked: reading the remediation diff beside the pass-one one-line fix, then running the owning test file.\\n- Prefer for: every remaining pass-one finding in this area.\\n\\n### String-containment marker scan -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, one attempt)\\n- What was tried: keeping the old `JSON.stringify(payload).includes(marker)` check.\\n- Why blocked: it passes a description-only mention, which is the pass-one DR5-P2-002 defect.\\n- Do NOT retry: match the serialized payload; walk `type: command` entries instead.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Swept: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n- The pass-one DR1-P1-001 write-failure fix is incomplete -- ruled out: the engine restores, prints backup and undo, and exits 3; the remaining gap is the route text for a second restore fault (iteration 1, evidence: `agents-md-embed.cjs:1425-1439`).\\n- The pass-one DR4-P1-001 symlink fix misses the link-install mode -- ruled out: `compose` refuses the router and mirror when the action would write, and `assertWritable` refuses a link that resolves outside the root (iteration 1, evidence: `agents-md-embed.cjs:819-829`).\\n- A malformed router row still reads as missing -- ruled out: `parseTableRows` keeps the row and A11 prints its line and width (iteration 2, evidence: `agents-md-check.cjs:803-826`).\\n- The pass-one Q3 fix is complete -- not ruled out: the setup YAML names the absent state, but `setup.md:82` names the wrong switch (iteration 4, evidence: `metrics.ts:451-464`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Focus area: the four pass-one embed-engine fixes and the changed embed tests\\n- Reason: the engine is the only mutating surface in this area and its exit contract changed\\n- Required evidence: direct read of the changed ranges plus the owning test file\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n- The pass-one report (`review/review-report-pass-1.md`) lists 43 merged findings; 17 belong to this area, all P2 after verification.\\n- The remediation range is `320e7b64d4..HEAD` (HEAD `087888ec4a`); 21 doctor-install files changed.\\n- The pass-one lineage (`review/lineages/doctor-install/`) stopped at its five-iteration cap with a last novelty ratio of 0.125, so this pass exists to verify the fixes and converge.\\n- The doctor-install area touches four prompt-hook runtimes (claude, codex, cursor, devin); opencode, pi and dsh have no advisor hook entry in this checkout, and `hook-wiring-check.cjs` skips them by design.\\n- Holdout files belong to the accuracy-runner area. This lineage opened none and reports counts only where a doc mentions them.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | Packet docs read in iteration 4 |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | No checklist row claimed yet |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | - | No skill or agent definition in this area |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | Runtime coverage read in iteration 3 |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | Feature catalog describes the advisor, not the doctor routes |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | - | No playbook file in this area |\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n[Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\\n\\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\\n| [path/to/file] | [D1, D3] | [N] | [0 P0, 1 P1, 2 P2] | [partial/complete] |\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- Max iterations: 7\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.10\\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-doctor-install-2-1794570021136-noekp0, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\\n- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Severity threshold: 