{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571209184,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c777a4001vmYiL2Pij9yfQQ","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4c74f5b001QGzSJo1SqEipUO","type":"tool","id":"call_b4f72c33367b482d96f184b7","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading the remediation diff first, then the surrounding function, kept every pass-one verdict tied to the current bytes (iteration 1).\n- Running the changed `node --test` files gave a whole-gate baseline before any finding was recorded (iterations 1 to 4).\n- Probing `hook-wiring-check.cjs` with temporary hook fixtures exposed wrapper shapes the unit tests do not cover (iteration 3).\n- Comparing the setup leg's hook-health claim against `metrics.ts` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` found a surviving pass-one doc defect (iteration 4).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- The pass-one fix for the setup absent-hook-health message names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` as the switch that turns records on; the writer records every prompt by default and the flag only adds two fields (iteration 4).\n- The new exit-3 contract covers `restored:` and `nothing was restored` but not the engine's `the restore failed` path (iteration 1).\n- The narrowed hook-wiring matcher does not recognise `env node ...` or `bash -lc \"node ...\"` wrappers (iteration 3).","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -52,20 +52,15 @@\n \n <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n-- Reading the remediation diff first, then the surrounding function, kept every pass-one verdict tied to the current bytes (iteration 1).\n-- Running the changed `node --test` files gave a whole-gate baseline before any finding was recorded (iterations 1 to 4).\n-- Probing `hook-wiring-check.cjs` with temporary hook fixtures exposed wrapper shapes the unit tests do not cover (iteration 3).\n-- Comparing the setup leg's hook-health claim against `metrics.ts` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` found a surviving pass-one doc defect (iteration 4).\n+- [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-- The pass-one fix for the setup absent-hook-health message names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` as the switch that turns records on; the writer records every prompt by default and the flag only adds two fields (iteration 4).\n-- The new exit-3 contract covers `restored:` and `nothing was restored` but not the engine's `the restore failed` path (iteration 1).\n-- The narrowed hook-wiring matcher does not recognise `env node ...` or `bash -lc \"node ...\"` wrappers (iteration 3).\n+- [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":7}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Reading the remediation diff first, then the surrounding function, kept every pass-one verdict tied to the current bytes (iteration 1).\\n- Running the changed `node --test` files gave a whole-gate baseline before any finding was recorded (iterations 1 to 4).\\n- Probing `hook-wiring-check.cjs` with temporary hook fixtures exposed wrapper shapes the unit tests do not cover (iteration 3).\\n- Comparing the setup leg's hook-health claim against `metrics.ts` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` found a surviving pass-one doc defect (iteration 4).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- The pass-one fix for the setup absent-hook-health message names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` as the switch that turns records on; the writer records every prompt by default and the flag only adds two fields (iteration 4).\\n- The new exit-3 contract covers `restored:` and `nothing was restored` but not the engine's `the restore failed` path (iteration 1).\\n- The narrowed hook-wiring matcher does not recognise `env node ...` or `bash -lc \\\"node ...\\\"` wrappers (iteration 3).\",\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571204516,"end":1794571209184}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571209193,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c78124001RY2QbpKJj6CI23","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4c74f5b001QGzSJo1SqEipUO","type":"tool","id":"call_29b852adc4ef42ecbe189b2a","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n- The pass-one DR1-P1-001 write-failure fix is incomplete -- ruled out: the engine restores, prints backup and undo, and exits 3; the remaining gap is the route text for a second restore fault (iteration 1, evidence: `agents-md-embed.cjs:1425-1439`).\n- The pass-one DR4-P1-001 symlink fix misses the link-install mode -- ruled out: `compose` refuses the router and mirror when the action would write, and `assertWritable` refuses a link that resolves outside the root (iteration 1, evidence: `agents-md-embed.cjs:819-829`).\n- A malformed router row still reads as missing -- ruled out: `parseTableRows` keeps the row and A11 prints its line and width (iteration 2, evidence: `agents-md-check.cjs:803-826`).\n- The pass-one Q3 fix is complete -- not ruled out: the setup YAML names the absent state, but `setup.md:82` names the wrong switch (iteration 4, evidence: `metrics.ts:451-464`).","newString":"## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n- [Populated as iterations complete]"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md\n===