{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571361111,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c9d17f001Ajr8H5CXurFUBD","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4c9bdea0011VQNbRYQJfpvnk","type":"tool","id":"call_25ce2be8d5bd4eb490dbc1c3","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading the remediation diff beside the pass-one one-line fix, then running the owning test file, kept every verdict tied to the bytes as they are now (iteration 1).\n- Running the check engine against this checkout and its test file beside the changed verdict branches proved the five check-engine fixes without a fixture-only claim (iteration 2).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- The new exit-3 contract covers `restored:` and `nothing was restored` but not the engine's `the restore failed` path, so the route has no branch for a partly written tree (iteration 1).\n- No check-engine fix failed in iteration 2. The one recorded limitation is the header assumption in `parseTableRows`, which every shipped router satisfies.","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading the remediation diff beside the pass-one one-line fix, then running the owning test file, kept every verdict tied to the bytes as they are now (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- The new exit-3 contract covers `restored:` and `nothing was restored` but not the engine's `the restore failed` path, so the route has no branch for a partly written tree (iteration 1).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -52,14 +52,16 @@\n <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n - Reading the remediation diff beside the pass-one one-line fix, then running the owning test file, kept every verdict tied to the bytes as they are now (iteration 1).\n+- Running the check engine against this checkout and its test file beside the changed verdict branches proved the five check-engine fixes without a fixture-only claim (iteration 2).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n - The new exit-3 contract covers `restored:` and `nothing was restored` but not the engine's `the restore failed` path, so the route has no branch for a partly written tree (iteration 1).\n+- No check-engine fix failed in iteration 2. The one recorded limitation is the header assumption in `parseTableRows`, which every shipped router satisfies.\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Reading the remediation diff beside the pass-one one-line fix, then running the owning test file, kept every verdict tied to the bytes as they are now (iteration 1).\\n- Running the check engine against this checkout and its test file beside the changed verdict branches proved the five check-engine fixes without a fixture-only claim (iteration 2).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- The new exit-3 contract covers `restored:` and `nothing was restored` but not the engine's `the restore failed` path, so the route has no branch for a partly written tree (iteration 1).\\n- No check-engine fix failed in iteration 2. The one recorded limitation is the header assumption in `parseTableRows`, which every shipped router satisfies.\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Reading the remediation diff beside the pass-one one-line fix, then running the owning test file, kept every verdict tied to the bytes as they are now (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- The new exit-3 contract covers `restored:` and `nothing was restored` but not the engine's `the restore failed` path, so the route has no branch for a partly written tree (iteration 1).\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571358591,"end":1794571361111}}}}
