{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571498298,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4cbf0b4002eVeT3c70CIoiLG","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4cbdab4001byKh295PSy1g6C","type":"tool","id":"call_fa3b9debea814ff3b4603064","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"doctor\\|install\\|agents-md\\|setup\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md | head -30; wc -l specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md"},"output":"64:The repository ships 44 tracked slash commands that own complete workflows, but the skill advisor reaches the model with skills. Only `/doctor:*` commands arrive as a runnable line, 22 of 62 command bridge rows are off in the TypeScript scorer, the recommendation carries no command field and no rule tells a model what to do with a surfaced command. A user who chats without typing a command therefore gets an improvised approach where a command workflow exists. The evidence is in `../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/research.md` and the independent review `../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md`.\n79:- Generate one command inventory with a risk class and a derived policy per command and per doctor route.\n99:| `.skilled/skills/*/command-metadata.json`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` | Modify, Create | 002 | Risk class and write target per command and route |\n123:| 8 | 008-embedder-setup-and-cost/ | The embedder for external repositories: visible state, a plan-first doctor route, the measured memory and latency cost in the install guides and defined absent, cold and slow behaviour (operator requirement, 2026-11-12) | Complete |\n125:| 10 | 010-reachability-and-attribution/ | Offer and brief delivery on every run line with a backfill of the before arm, an attributable scorer summary, the Codex and DSH install steps with read-only doctor checks and a measured cold first prompt (research ranks 1 to 6 and 10) | Complete |\n127:| 12 | 012-plain-offer-reach/ | A plain request gets its command: the doctor hand-off names the command its ranker put first, task-shaped aliases on the `sk-doc` and deep-loop hubs, deep and create anchors and a `(needs a mode)` label for a deferring hub, measured as plain tune offers 9 to 23 of 45 in the command capture (segment two ranks 1, 4, 6, 7 and 12) | Complete |\n128:| 13 | 013-attribution-and-install-reach/ | Brief delivery as a stored fact on five runtimes, offer accounting with loop-without-init in the safety floor and host-expanded typed starts counted, a Codex preflight and a restore to HEAD in the behaviour runner, a `CLAUDE.md` pointer on the default embed install, a delivery leg in `/doctor:setup` and an OpenCode brief that keeps the command fields (segment two ranks 2, 3, 5, 8 to 11 and 13) | Complete |\n144:| 002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata | 003-plain-chat-command-reach | Every tracked command and doctor route has a risk class and a derived policy | The deriver's check mode is fresh and exits 1 on a fixture command with no metadata |\n148:| 006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers | 007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof | The Gate 2 sentence and the generated pointer are in place | `/doctor:agents-md check` passes and the pointer generator's check exits 0 |\n149:| 007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof | 008-embedder-setup-and-cost | Phase 005 is merged and the per-runtime proof is recorded, so this phase edits the final recommendation handler and bridge activation list | `rg -n \"ownerSkillId\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints a line and phase 007 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\n151:| 012-plain-offer-reach | 013-attribution-and-install-reach | Phase 012 is committed, its renderer prints `(needs a mode)` and its diff touches none of the files phase 013 edits | The committed command baseline reads `attachedMetrics.plain.tune.combined` above 9 of 45 and phase 012 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\n152:| 013-attribution-and-install-reach | 014-review-remediation | Review pass one is merged and verified, with its findings grouped into file-disjoint work groups | `review/review-report.md` holds the Planning Packet and phase 014 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\n162:- The review's G2 check, that a started command actually runs its own setup, is a condition of decision D1. If phase 7 shows setup being skipped, D1 returns to the operator.\n     171 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"64:The repository ships 44 tracked slash commands that own complete workflows, but the skill advisor reaches the model with skills. Only `/doctor:*` commands arrive as a runnable line, 22 of 62 command bridge rows are off in the TypeScript scorer, the recommendation carries no command field and no rule tells a model what to do with a surfaced command. A user who chats without typing a command therefore gets an improvised approach where a command workflow exists. The evidence is in `../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/research.md` and the independent review `../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md`.\n79:- Generate one command inventory with a risk class and a derived policy per command and per doctor route.\n99:| `.skilled/skills/*/command-metadata.json`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` | Modify, Create | 002 | Risk class and write target per command and route |\n123:| 8 | 008-embedder-setup-and-cost/ | The embedder for external repositories: visible state, a plan-first doctor route, the measured memory and latency cost in the install guides and defined absent, cold and slow behaviour (operator requirement, 2026-11-12) | Complete |\n125:| 10 | 010-reachability-and-attribution/ | Offer and brief delivery on every run line with a backfill of the before arm, an attributable scorer summary, the Codex and DSH install steps with read-only doctor checks and a measured cold first prompt (research ranks 1 to 6 and 10) | Complete |\n127:| 12 | 012-plain-offer-reach/ | A plain request gets its command: the doctor hand-off names the command its ranker put first, task-shaped aliases on the `sk-doc` and deep-loop hubs, deep and create anchors and a `(needs a mode)` label for a deferring hub, measured as plain tune offers 9 to 23 of 45 in the command capture (segment two ranks 1, 4, 6, 7 and 12) | Complete |\n128:| 13 | 013-attribution-and-install-reach/ | Brief delivery as a stored fact on five runtimes, offer accounting with loop-without-init in the safety floor and host-expanded typed starts counted, a Codex preflight and a restore to HEAD in the behaviour runner, a `CLAUDE.md` pointer on the default embed install, a delivery leg in `/doctor:setup` and an OpenCode brief that keeps the command fields (segment two ranks 2, 3, 5, 8 to 11 and 13) | Complete |\n144:| 002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata | 003-plain-chat-command-reach | Every tracked command and doctor route has a risk class and a derived policy | The deriver's check mode is fresh and exits 1 on a fixture command with no metadata |\n148:| 006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers | 007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof | The Gate 2 sentence and the generated pointer are in place | `/doctor:agents-md check` passes and the pointer generator's check exits 0 |\n149:| 007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof | 008-embedder-setup-and-cost | Phase 005 is merged and the per-runtime proof is recorded, so this phase edits the final recommendation handler and bridge activation list | `rg -n \"ownerSkillId\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints a line and phase 007 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\n151:| 012-plain-offer-reach | 013-attribution-and-install-reach | Phase 012 is committed, its renderer prints `(needs a mode)` and its diff touches none of the files phase 013 edits | The committed command baseline reads `attachedMetrics.plain.tune.combined` above 9 of 45 and phase 012 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\n152:| 013-attribution-and-install-reach | 014-review-remediation | Review pass one is merged and verified, with its findings grouped into file-disjoint work groups | `review/review-report.md` holds the Planning Packet and phase 014 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\n162:- The review's G2 check, that a started command actually runs its own setup, is a condition of decision D1. If phase 7 shows setup being skipped, D1 returns to the operator.\n     171 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"doctor\\\\|install\\\\|agents-md\\\\|setup\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md | head -30; wc -l specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571497652,"end":1794571498298}}}}
