14-review-remediation | 015-health-default-and-brief-refinements | Phase 014 is committed and every pinned floor holds | The command capture prints typed recall 24 of 44 and false offers 0 of 35, and phase 014 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\n154: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-map -->\n155: \n156: ---\n157: \n158: <!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n159: ## 4. OPEN QUESTIONS\n160: \n161: - Phase 7 needs runs on runtimes the research never exercised live (Pi, Cursor, Devin, DSH, Codex, OpenCode). Which of them the operator wants proven is decided when phase 7 is planned.\n162: - The review's G2 check, that a started command actually runs its own setup, is a condition of decision D1. If phase 7 shows setup being skipped, D1 returns to the operator.\n163: <!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n164: \n165: ---\n166: \n167: ## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n168: \n169: - **Phase children**: See sub-folders `[0-9][0-9][0-9]-*/` for per-phase spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md\n170: - **Parent Spec**: See `../spec.md`\n171: - **Graph Metadata**: See `graph-metadata.json` for `derived.last_active_child_id` pointer","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md, lines 132-171\n132: ### Phase Transition Rules\n133: \n134: - Each phase MUST pass `validate.sh` independently before the next phase begins\n135: - Parent spec tracks aggregate progress via this map\n136: - Use `/speckit:resume [parent-folder]/[NNN-phase]/` to resume a specific phase\n137: - Run `validate.sh --recursive` on parent to validate all phases as integrated unit\n138: \n139: ### Phase Handoff Criteria\n140: \n141: | From | To | Criteria | Verification |\n142: |------|-----|----------|--------------|\n143: | 001-command-routing-baseline-corpus | 002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata | Corpus rows exist for all 44 tracked commands and a baseline records per-command recall, with the four existing numbers unchanged | The baseline file exists and the existing routing-accuracy run still reports 158/195, 50/66 and 20/24 |\n144: | 002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata | 003-plain-chat-command-reach | Every tracked command and doctor route has a risk class and a derived policy | The deriver's check mode is fresh and exits 1 on a fixture command with no metadata |\n145: | 003-plain-chat-command-reach | 004-command-meaning-matching | Command recall rises against the phase 1 baseline with no drop in the four existing numbers | The phase 1 scorer run, and no typed command is ambiguous with its own owner |\n146: | 004-command-meaning-matching | 005-recommendation-contract-and-brief | Holdout plain recall rises above 0 of 44 with false offers at 0 of 35 and typed recall at least 24 of 44, measured with the real embedding | The real-embedding capture and the full advisor suite |\n147: | 005-recommendation-contract-and-brief | 006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers | The recommendation and the brief carry the command and its policy | Schema test and golden briefs pass, and `save context` returns one entry |\n148: | 006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers | 007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof | The Gate 2 sentence and the generated pointer are in place | `/doctor:agents-md check` passes and the pointer generator's check exits 0 |\n149: | 007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof | 008-embedder-setup-and-cost | Phase 005 is merged and the per-runtime proof is recorded, so this phase edits the final recommendation handler and bridge activation list | `rg -n \"ownerSkillId\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints a line and phase 007 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\n150: | 011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards | 012-plain-offer-reach | Phase 011 is committed, the command capture reads 44 of 44 typed rows and every pinned floor holds | `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` prints `combined` 44 of 44 and phase 011 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\n151: | 012-plain-offer-reach | 013-attribution-and-install-reach | Phase 012 is committed, its renderer prints `(needs a mode)` and its diff touches none of the files phase 013 edits | The committed command baseline reads `attachedMetrics.plain.tune.combined` above 9 of 45 and phase 012 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\n152: | 013-attribution-and-install-reach | 014-review-remediation | Review pass one is merged and verified, with its findings grouped into file-disjoint work groups | `review/review-report.md` holds the Planning Packet and phase 014 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\n153: | 014-review-remediation | 015-health-default-and-brief-refinements | Phase 014 is committed and every pinned floor holds | The command capture prints typed recall 24 of 44 and false offers 0 of 35, and phase 014 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\n154: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-map -->\n155: \n156: ---\n157: \n158: <!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n159: ## 4. OPEN QUESTIONS\n160: \n161: - Phase 7 needs runs on runtimes the research never exercised live (Pi, Cursor, Devin, DSH, Codex, OpenCode). Which of them the operator wants proven is decided when phase 7 is planned.\n162: - The review's G2 check, that a started command actually runs its own setup, is a condition of decision D1. If phase 7 shows setup being skipped, D1 returns to the operator.\n163: <!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n164: \n165: ---\n166: \n167: ## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n168: \n169: - **Phase children**: See sub-folders `[0-9][0-9][0-9]-*/` for per-phase spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md\n170: - **Parent Spec**: See `../spec.md`\n171: - **Graph Metadata**: See `graph-metadata.json` for `derived.last_active_child_id` pointer"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":40,\"offset\":132,\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571503962,"end":1794571504455}}}}
