{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571777403,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4cfd479001pQuWy86Q2Hkmjc","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4cf8107001uHw5SN6dj1AOYV","type":"tool","id":"call_f2bbeaec0cc14deba7ae9d35","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 5 — maintainability and traceability\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review; target agent `@deep-review`; detached fan-out lineage `doctor-install`.\n- Session: `fanout-doctor-install-2-1794570021136-noekp0`, generation 1, lineageMode new.\n- Artifact root: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2`.\n- Dimension: maintainability and traceability. Budget profile: verify.\n- Operator review focus: pass two of the command-surfacing review. This iteration read the remaining unchanged doctor-install files that describe or route the changed surfaces and checked the A10 row against its own manifest. It addressed the docs-that-disagree-with-code part of the focus and the claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh surfaces named in the route manifest. No holdout file was opened.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:512-541` (check and embed routes, mutation class, gate-3 location, script invocations)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md:80-90` (workflow summary)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json` (`runtime_copies`, including the report-only entries at `:758` and `:777`)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:636-654` (A10 count and detail)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs:576-600` (the count the test pins)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:150-180` (output and repair routing)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt:230-245` (embedder plan rows)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md:55-75` (embedder target routing)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh:960-990` (shared spec-create surface; no doctor route)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:370-385`, `INSTALL-SKILLED.md:120-155`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **A10 counts report-only entries among the \"copies as expected\"** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:651` -- the row subtracts failed, unmeasured and pointer-missing entries from the expected count, but two INFO entries with `kind: 'reported only'` (`.cursorrules` and `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, both `report_only: true` in `agents-md-manifest.json`) remain in the numerator. In this checkout A10 prints `5/6 copies as expected, 1 pointer missing` while only three of the six entries are PASS; the two report-only paths were never read. The pass-one DR3-P2-001 fix excluded the pointer-missing INFO entry but left the other INFO class in the count.\n   Case: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs --root .` prints `A10 runtime copies: 5/6 copies as expected, 1 pointer missing (PASS)`; the JSON entries show `CLAUDE.md` INFO pointer missing, `.cursorrules` INFO reported only and `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` INFO reported only, so five \"expected\" copies include two paths the check says it never read.\n   Finding class: misleading-evidence\n   Scope proof: `rowRuntimeCopies` computes `expected` from `entries.length - failed - unmeasured - pointerMissing` at `:651`; neither `report_only` nor `kind === 'reported only'` is subtracted, and the test at `agents-md-check.test.cjs:576-600` pins the 5/6 detail.\n   Affected surface hints: [\"A10 runtime copies\", \"report-only manifest entries\", \"doctor agents-md check\"]\n   Claim adjudication: `{\"type\":\"traceability\",\"claim\":\"A10's expected count includes entries its own details classify as report-only, so the numerator claims a checked copy that was never read.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:651\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:758\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:777\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"read the manifest entries and the row loop; report_only returns INFO and the loop prints only FINDING, UNKNOWN and pointer missing, so a report-only entry is invisible except in the count\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"as expected may mean expected behaviour of every entry, but the same row separates pointer missing for exactly the opposite reason, so the count reads as checked copies\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P2\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"a documented definition that as expected includes report-only entries\"}`\n\n2. **The embed route names the backup folder `<timestamp>` while the engine names it by plan digest and may fall back outside the repository** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:536` -- the route's gate-3 location says a copy of every touched path is taken to `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/`. `planFor` names the directory from the first 16 characters of the plan digest (`agents-md-embed.cjs:954-956`, `:997-1005`), and `backupBase` falls back to `os.tmpdir()/doctor-agents-md` when git does not ignore the output base (`:967-983`). The plan itself prints the actual `backup:` path, so the operator can recover, but the route's stated path is wrong in both its name and its location.\n   Case: a fixture with no `.skilled/output` ignore rule: `agents-md-embed.cjs plan --root <dir>` prints `backup: /var/folders/.../doctor-agents-md/<16-hex>` while `_routes.yaml:536` tells the reader to look under `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/`.\n   Finding class: documentation-drift\n   Scope proof: `rg -n \"timestamp|plan digest|backupDirectoryOf|BACKUP_FALLBACK_DIR\" agents-md-embed.cjs` shows the digest slice and the temp fallback; the route's `<timestamp>` appears only in `_routes.yaml:536`.\n   Affected surface hints: [\"agents-md embed route\", \"gate-3 location\", \"backup and undo lines\"]\n   Claim adjudication: `{\"type\":\"traceability\",\"claim\":\"The route's backup path contract does not match the engine's directory name or its fallback.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:536\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:954\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:982\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"read planFor, backupBase and renderPlan; the plan prints backup: from plan.dir and the directory is the digest slice\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"the timestamp may be the record's created_at inside the folder, but the folder segment is the digest and the route says the folder is timestamped\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P2\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"a documented decision that <timestamp> names the record's created_at rather than the directory\"}`\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-------|\n| spec_code | core | pass | The route manifest and the parent spec place the embed route in the command-surfacing scope; the docs/code mismatches above are inside that scope. |\n| checklist_evidence | core | notApplicable | The parent has no checklist; phase children own theirs. |\n| skill_agent | overlay | notApplicable | No skill or agent definition in this area. |\n| agent_cross_runtime | overlay | pass | The route manifest names the same six runtimes as `symlink-manifest.json`; dsh has no install row. |\n| feature_catalog_code | overlay | notApplicable | The advisor feature catalog does not describe the doctor routes. |\n| playbook_capability | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook file in this area. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- The `agents-md-check.cjs --json` output was read directly for the A10 entries; the two report-only entries and the pointer-missing entry are visible in the JSON but not in the printed lines.\n- The engine's plan output was compared with `_routes.yaml:536`; `backupDirectoryOf` and `backupBase` settle the directory name and fallback.\n- `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root .` remains `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor`, `ok devin`; no route file was executed as a mutating command.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The `.cursorrules` entry is report-only because that file shape is outside the checklist this command rewrites; it is still an entry in the same A10 row, so the count question applies to it.\n- `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` is a home-directory path, not a path under the target root; `copyVerdict` returns INFO before it joins the path, so the check never reads the user's home file. That is the right behaviour for a repository-scoped check; the count is the only defect.\n- The route's `<timestamp>` is also inaccurate when the backup stays under `.skilled/output`: the folder segment is the digest slice, not a clock reading.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:165-170` routes an absent Codex entry to the repair line the check prints and keeps the DSH rows `n/a` while the tree is absent; the YAML is unchanged and consistent with the check.\n- `doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt:230-245` prints the embedder plan with the install/start/pull rows and their undo; it does not claim a hook-health result.\n- `skill-advisor.md:55-75` binds the `embedder` target to the YAML and the presentation contract; the target list matches `_routes.yaml`.\n- `agents-md.md:80-90` summarizes plan, approval, write, re-read and restore without contradicting the engine's exit contract; its dropped-line sentence is a subset, not a false universal.\n- `create.sh` carries no doctor route; it is in this area as a shared spec-create surface and no finding depends on it.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **The manifest report-only entries are written by the engine** -- ruled out: `copyVerdict` returns INFO before any path join, and the embed allowlist does not include `~/.claude` or `.cursorrules`.\n- **The backup always lands under `.skilled/output`** -- not ruled out: `backupBase` falls back to `os.tmpdir()/doctor-agents-md` when the output base is not ignored; this is part of the route finding above.\n- **A10's 5/6 count is only the pointer-missing decision** -- ruled out: the pointer-missing fix is correct, but two report-only entries remain in the numerator (iteration 5, evidence: `agents-md-check.cjs:651`).\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability and cross-reference\n- Focus area: final consistency pass over the five P2 findings, the reducer registry, and the convergence vote\n- Reason: all changed and unchanged area files have been read; the next iteration verifies the finding evidence and the state before synthesis.\n- Rotation status: all four dimensions covered; coverage changed this iteration, so one stabilization pass remains.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: do not re-open the five findings unless a re-read contradicts them.\n- Required evidence: registry counts, iteration final lines, and a final read of each finding's cited line.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 5 — maintainability and traceability\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review; target agent `@deep-review`; detached fan-out lineage `doctor-install`.\\n- Session: `fanout-doctor-install-2-1794570021136-noekp0`, generation 1, lineageMode new.\\n- Artifact root: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2`.\\n- Dimension: maintainability and traceability. Budget profile: verify.\\n- Operator review focus: pass two of the command-surfacing review. This iteration read the remaining unchanged doctor-install files that describe or route the changed surfaces and checked the A10 row against its own manifest. It addressed the docs-that-disagree-with-code part of the focus and the claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh surfaces named in the route manifest. No holdout file was opened.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:512-541` (check and embed routes, mutation class, gate-3 location, script invocations)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md:80-90` (workflow summary)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json` (`runtime_copies`, including the report-only entries at `:758` and `:777`)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:636-654` (A10 count and detail)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs:576-600` (the count the test pins)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:150-180` (output and repair routing)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt:230-245` (embedder plan rows)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md:55-75` (embedder target routing)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh:960-990` (shared spec-create surface; no doctor route)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:370-385`, `INSTALL-SKILLED.md:120-155`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **A10 counts report-only entries among the \\\"copies as expected\\\"** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:651` -- the row subtracts failed, unmeasured and pointer-missing entries from the expected count, but two INFO entries with `kind: 'reported only'` (`.cursorrules` and `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, both `report_only: true` in `agents-md-manifest.json`) remain in the numerator. In this checkout A10 prints `5/6 copies as expected, 1 pointer missing` while only three of the six entries are PASS; the two report-only paths were never read. The pass-one DR3-P2-001 fix excluded the pointer-missing INFO entry but left the other INFO class in the count.\\n   Case: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs --root .` prints `A10 runtime copies: 5/6 copies as expected, 1 pointer missing (PASS)`; the JSON entries show `CLAUDE.md` INFO pointer missing, `.cursorrules` INFO reported only and `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` INFO reported only, so five \\\"expected\\\" copies include two paths the check says it never read.\\n   Finding class: misleading-evidence\\n   Scope proof: `rowRuntimeCopies` computes `expected` from `entries.length - failed - unmeasured - pointerMissing` at `:651`; neither `report_only` nor `kind === 'reported only'` is subtracted, and the test at `agents-md-check.test.cjs:576-600` pins the 5/6 detail.\\n   Affected surface hints: [\\\"A10 runtime copies\\\", \\\"report-only manifest entries\\\", \\\"doctor agents-md check\\\"]\\n   Claim adjudication: `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"traceability\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"A10's expected count includes entries its own details classify as report-only, so the numerator claims a checked copy that was never read.\\\",\\\"evidenceRefs\\\":[\\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:651\\\",\\\".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:758\\\",\\\".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:777\\\"],\\\"counterevidenceSought\\\":\\\"read the manifest entries and the row loop; report_only returns INFO and the loop prints only FINDING, UNKNOWN and pointer missing, so a report-only entry is invisible except in the count\\\",\\\"alternativeExplanation\\\":\\\"as expected may mean expected behaviour of every entry, but the same row separates pointer missing for exactly the opposite reason, so the count reads as checked copies\\\",\\\"finalSeverity\\\":\\\"P2\\\",\\\"confidence\\\":0.9,\\\"downgradeTrigger\\\":\\\"a documented definition that as expected includes report-only entries\\\"}`\\n\\n2. **The embed route names the backup folder `<timestamp>` while the engine names it by plan digest and may fall back outside the repository** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:536` -- the route's gate-3 location says a copy of every touched path is taken to `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/`. `planFor` names the directory from the first 16 characters of the plan digest (`agents-md-embed.cjs:954-956`, `:997-1005`), and `backupBase` falls back to `os.tmpdir()/doctor-agents-md` when git does not ignore the output base (`:967-983`). The plan itself prints the actual `backup:` path, so the operator can recover, but the route's stated path is wrong in both its name and its location.\\n   Case: a fixture with no `.skilled/output` ignore rule: `agents-md-embed.cjs plan --root <dir>` prints `backup: /var/folders/.../doctor-agents-md/<16-hex>` while `_routes.yaml:536` tells the reader to look under `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/`.\\n   Finding class: documentation-drift\\n   Scope proof: `rg -n \\\"timestamp|plan digest|backupDirectoryOf|BACKUP_FALLBACK_DIR\\\" agents-md-embed.cjs` shows the digest slice and the temp fallback; the route's `<timestamp>` appears only in `_routes.yaml:536`.\\n   Affected surface hints: [\\\"agents-md embed route\\\", \\\"gate-3 location\\\", \\\"backup and undo lines\\\"]\\n   Claim adjudication: `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"traceability\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"The route's backup path contract does not match the engine's directory name or its fallback.\\\",\\\"evidenceRefs\\\":[\\\".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:536\\\",\\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:954\\\",\\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:982\\\"],\\\"counterevidenceSought\\\":\\\"read planFor, backupBase and renderPlan; the plan prints backup: from plan.dir and the directory is the digest slice\\\",\\\"alternativeExplanation\\\":\\\"the timestamp may be the record's created_at inside the folder, but the folder segment is the digest and the route says the folder is timestamped\\\",\\\"finalSeverity\\\":\\\"P2\\\",\\\"confidence\\\":0.9,\\\"downgradeTrigger\\\":\\\"a documented decision that <timestamp> names the record's created_at rather than the directory\\\"}`\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-------|\\n| spec_code | core | pass | The route manifest and the parent spec place the embed route in the command-surfacing scope; the docs/code mismatches above are inside that scope. |\\n| checklist_evidence | core | notApplicable | The parent has no checklist; phase children own theirs. |\\n| skill_agent | overlay | notApplicable | No skill or agent definition in this area. |\\n| agent_cross_runtime | overlay | pass | The route manifest names the same six runtimes as `symlink-manifest.json`; dsh has no install row. |\\n| feature_catalog_code | overlay | notApplicable | The advisor feature catalog does not describe the doctor routes. |\\n| playbook_capability | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook file in this area. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- The `agents-md-check.cjs --json` output was read directly for the A10 entries; the two report-only entries and the pointer-missing entry are visible in the JSON but not in the printed lines.\\n- The engine's plan output was compared with `_routes.yaml:536`; `backupDirectoryOf` and `backupBase` settle the directory name and fallback.\\n- `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root .` remains `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor`, `ok devin`; no route file was executed as a mutating command.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The `.cursorrules` entry is report-only because that file shape is outside the checklist this command rewrites; it is still an entry in the same A10 row, so the count question applies to it.\\n- `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` is a home-directory path, not a path under the target root; `copyVerdict` returns INFO before it joins the path, so the check never reads the user's home file. That is the right behaviour for a repository-scoped check; the count is the only defect.\\n- The route's `<timestamp>` is also inaccurate when the backup stays under `.skilled/output`: the folder segment is the digest slice, not a clock reading.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:165-170` routes an absent Codex entry to the repair line the check prints and keeps the DSH rows `n/a` while the tree is absent; the YAML is unchanged and consistent with the check.\\n- `doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt:230-245` prints the embedder plan with the install/start/pull rows and their undo; it does not claim a hook-health result.\\n- `skill-advisor.md:55-75` binds the `embedder` target to the YAML and the presentation contract; the target list matches `_routes.yaml`.\\n- `agents-md.md:80-90` summarizes plan, approval, write, re-read and restore without contradicting the engine's exit contract; its dropped-line sentence is a subset, not a false universal.\\n- `create.sh` carries no doctor route; it is in this area as a shared spec-create surface and no finding depends on it.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **The manifest report-only entries are written by the engine** -- ruled out: `copyVerdict` returns INFO before any path join, and the embed allowlist does not include `~/.claude` or `.cursorrules`.\\n- **The backup always lands under `.skilled/output`** -- not ruled out: `backupBase` falls back to `os.tmpdir()/doctor-agents-md` when the output base is not ignored; this is part of the route finding above.\\n- **A10's 5/6 count is only the pointer-missing decision** -- ruled out: the pointer-missing fix is correct, but two report-only entries remain in the numerator (iteration 5, evidence: `agents-md-check.cjs:651`).\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability and cross-reference\\n- Focus area: final consistency pass over the five P2 findings, the reducer registry, and the convergence vote\\n- Reason: all changed and unchanged area files have been read; the next iteration verifies the finding evidence and the state before synthesis.\\n- Rotation status: all four dimensions covered; coverage changed this iteration, so one stabilization pass remains.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: do not re-open the five findings unless a re-read contradicts them.\\n- Required evidence: registry counts, iteration final lines, and a final read of each finding's cited line.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571752569,"end":1794571777403}}}}
