{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571789033,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4d054490015LKyNbGpHGg5B6","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4d03ee2001hFwZW8Dab43aVG","type":"tool","id":"call_12d85a2b49e44730808b2d13","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Comparing the setup leg's hook-health claim against `metrics.ts` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` found a surviving pass-one doc defect (iteration 4).\n- Reading the remaining route manifest and the A10 JSON entries found two docs-versus-code gaps the changed rows did not cover (iteration 5).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- The new exit-3 contract covers `restored:` and `nothing was restored` but not the engine's `the restore failed` path, so the route has no branch for a partly written tree (iteration 1).\n- No check-engine fix failed in iteration 2. The one recorded limitation is the header assumption in `parseTableRows`, which every shipped router satisfies.\n- The narrowed hook-wiring matcher does not recognise `env node ...`, `node --no-warnings ...` or `bash -lc \"node ...\"` wrappers (iteration 3).\n- The pass-one Q3 repair names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` as the switch that turns hook-health records on; the writer records every prompt by default and the flag only adds two fields (iteration 4).\n- A10 still counts report-only INFO entries as \"copies as expected\", and the embed route names the backup folder `<timestamp>` where the engine uses the plan digest (iteration 5).","oldString":"- Comparing the setup leg's hook-health claim against `metrics.ts` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` found a surviving pass-one doc defect (iteration 4).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- The new exit-3 contract covers `restored:` and `nothing was restored` but not the engine's `the restore failed` path, so the route has no branch for a partly written tree (iteration 1).\n- No check-engine fix failed in iteration 2. The one recorded limitation is the header ass