{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794572179468,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4d656a4001PceQfkLOkFvbyv","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a18a6ffeJYEGLs0dTSiOZ0","messageID":"msg_1d4d64075001OHe9iMDywD2zSi","type":"tool","id":"call_09c5488446df4d1b93f22d65","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-276\n1: # Deep Review Strategy - Doctor Install Pass Two\n2: \n3: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n4: \n5: - Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder), area `doctor-install`.\n6: - Purpose: verify every pass-one doctor-install fix holds, review every file changed since pass one line by line, then look for new defects.\n7: - Mutability: updated by the orchestrator and by each iteration; reducer-owned counts are refreshed after every iteration.\n8: \n9: ---\n10: \n11: ## 2. TOPIC\n12: \n13: Review: command surfacing pass two, doctor-install lineage. Scope is the doctor install, setup, symlink, runtime-mirrors and AGENTS.md routes plus the scripts and tests they own.\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n18: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n19: [All dimensions complete]\n20: \n21: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n22: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n23: \n24: - Re-report a pass-one finding whose fix holds, a deferred item from report section 8, R4-P2-003, or the refuted finding.\n25: - Review any file outside the 30 doctor-install area paths.\n26: - Read or print holdout prompt text. The doctor-install area opens no holdout file.\n27: - Change code. This lineage writes only its own review packet.\n28: \n29: ---\n30: \n31: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n32: \n33: - Composite convergence score at or above 0.60 with all four dimensions covered, or seven iterations.\n34: - A P0 or P1 finding keeps the verdict at FAIL or CONDITIONAL; it never blocks recording the iteration.\n35: \n36: ---\n37: \n38: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n39: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n40: - [x] correctness\n41: - [x] security\n42: - [x] traceability\n43: - [x] maintainability\n44: \n45: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n46: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n47: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n48: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n49: - P1 (Required): 0\n50: - P2 (Suggestions): 5\n51: - Resolved: 0\n52: \n53: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n54: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n55: \n56: - Reading the remediation diff beside the pass-one one-line fix, then running the owning test file, kept every verdict tied to the bytes as they are now (iteration 1).\n57: - Running the check engine against this checkout and its test file beside the changed verdict branches proved the five check-engine fixes without a fixture-only claim (iteration 2).\n58: - Probing `hook-wiring-check.cjs` with temporary hook fixtures exposed wrapper shapes the unit tests do not cover (iteration 3).\n59: - Comparing the setup leg's hook-health claim against `metrics.ts` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` found a surviving pass-one doc defect (iteration 4).\n60: - Reading the remaining route manifest and the A10 JSON entries found two docs-versus-code gaps the changed rows did not cover (iteration 5).\n61: - Re-reading every cited finding line and the owning test files confirmed all five findings and no pass-one regression (iteration 6).\n62: \n63: ---\n64: \n65: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n66: \n67: - The new exit-3 contract covers `restored:` and `nothing was restored` but not the engine's `the restore failed` path, so the route has no branch for a partly written tree (iteration 1).\n68: - No check-engine fix failed in iteration 2. The one recorded limitation is the header assumption in `parseTableRows`, which every shipped router satisfies.\n69: - The narrowed hook-wiring matcher does not recognise `env node ...`, `node --no-warnings ...` or `bash -lc \"node ...\"` wrappers (iteration 3).\n70: - The pass-one Q3 repair names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` as the switch that turns hook-health records on; the writer records every prompt by default and the flag only adds two fields (iteration 4).\n71: - A10 still counts report-only INFO entries as \"copies as expected\", and the embed route names the backup folder `<timestamp>` where the engine uses the plan digest (iteration 5).\n72: - No new defect appeared in the final consistency pass; the remaining debt is the five P2 findings, not a failed fix.\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n77: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n78: ### **`setup.md` documents an out-of-repository write the workflow forbids** -- ruled out: the workflow invariant names the socket directory and the setup.md prose names the same directory (iteration 4, evidence: `doctor-setup.yaml:28`). -- BLOCKED (iteration 4, 1 attempts)\n79: - What was tried: **`setup.md` documents an out-of-repository write the workflow forbids** -- ruled out: the workflow invariant names the socket directory and the setup.md prose names the same directory (iteration 4, evidence: `doctor-setup.yaml:28`).\n80: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n81: - Do NOT retry: **`setup.md` documents an out-of-repository write the workflow forbids** -- ruled out: the workflow invariant names the socket directory and the setup.md prose names the same directory (iteration 4, evidence: `doctor-setup.yaml:28`).\n82: \n83: ### **A flag value can still swallow the next option** -- ruled out: both checks refuse a value starting with `-` (iteration 3, evidence: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:58-62`). -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, 1 attempts)\n84: - What was tried: **A flag value can still swallow the next option** -- ruled out: both checks refuse a value starting with `-` (iteration 3, evidence: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:58-62`).\n85: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n86: - Do NOT retry: **A flag value can still swallow the next option** -- ruled out: both checks refuse a value starting with `-` (iteration 3, evidence: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:58-62`).\n87: \n88: ### **A hash-mismatched backup is still copied over the tree** -- ruled out: the pre-verification returns `null` before the copy loop, and the test asserts the damaged bytes never reach the root file. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n89: - What was tried: **A hash-mismatched backup is still copied over the tree** -- ruled out: the pre-verification returns `null` before the copy loop, and the test asserts the damaged bytes never reach the root file.\n90: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n91: - Do NOT retry: **A hash-mismatched backup is still copied over the tree** -- ruled out: the pre-verification returns `null` before the copy loop, and the test asserts the damaged bytes never reach the root file.\n92: \n93: ### **A malformed router row still reads as missing** -- ruled out: the row is kept, `missingRows` still finds its rule cell, and A11 prints the malformed line with its line number and width (iteration 2, evidence: `agents-md-check.cjs:803-826`). -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n94: - What was tried: **A malformed router row still reads as missing** -- ruled out: the row is kept, `missingRows` still finds its rule cell, and A11 prints the malformed line with its line number and width (iteration 2, evidence: `agents-md-check.cjs:803-826`).\n95: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n96: - Do NOT retry: **A malformed router row still reads as missing** -- ruled out: the row is kept, `missingRows` still finds its rule cell, and A11 prints the malformed line with its line number and width (iteration 2, evidence: `agents-md-check.cjs:803-826`).\n97: \n98: ### **A marker mentione