sal misses a link the run would remove -- ruled out: the action filter includes `remove`, and `restoreFromBackup` re-checks every path through `assertWritable` (iteration 1, evidence: `agents-md-embed.cjs:819-829`).\n201: - A hash-mismatched backup is still copied over the tree -- ruled out: the pre-verification returns `null` before the copy loop (iteration 1, evidence: `agents-md-embed.cjs:1313-1321`).\n202: - A malformed router row still reads as missing -- ruled out: the row is kept, its rule cell still resolves, and A11 prints the malformed line with its width (iteration 2, evidence: `agents-md-check.cjs:803-826`).\n203: - The pointer-missing count still includes the missing pointer -- ruled out: the count subtracts it and the test pins `5/6 ... 1 pointer missing` (iteration 2, evidence: `agents-md-check.cjs:649-653`).\n204: - A symlink at an absent-only path still passes -- ruled out: `expectsAbsent` is read before the symlink verdict (iteration 2, evidence: `agents-md-check.cjs:713-719`).\n205: - A marker mentioned only in a description still counts as wired -- ruled out: `collectCommands` reads `command` entries, and the description-only test reports `hook-missing` (iteration 3, evidence: `hook-wiring-check.cjs:114-122`).\n206: - An absent Codex entry still routes to a command that only reads -- ruled out: the check prints the copy-and-approve repair and the setup text routes to it (iteration 3, evidence: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:171-183`).\n207: - The symlink-check output block still omits the hook-wiring exits -- ruled out: WARN, FAIL and the worse-status rule are present (iteration 3, evidence: `doctor-symlink-check.yaml:69-72`).\n208: - The install route still says \"the seven\" -- ruled out: the presentation names the six runtimes and the contract test rejects the count phrase (iteration 4, evidence: `doctor-install-presentation.txt:78`).\n209: - The embedder start and pull ignore the resolved host -- ruled out: both bind `OLLAMA_HOST` and the non-local refusal comes first (iteration 4, evidence: `doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml:125-127`).\n210: - `setup.md` documents an out-of-repository write the workflow forbids -- ruled out: both name the socket directory (iteration 4, evidence: `doctor-setup.yaml:28`).\n211: - The manifest report-only entries are written by the engine -- ruled out: `copyVerdict` returns INFO before any path join and the embed allowlist excludes those paths (iteration 5, evidence: `agents-md-check.cjs:658-663`).\n212: - A10's 5/6 count is only the pointer-missing decision -- ruled out: the pointer fix is correct, but two report-only entries remain in the numerator (iteration 5, evidence: `agents-md-check.cjs:651`).\n213: - A pass-one fix regressed -- ruled out: each fix was re-read and its owning test file passed (iteration 6, evidence: `iteration-001.md` to `iteration-005.md`).\n214: - A new P0 or P1 exists in the area -- ruled out: the five findings are documentation or diagnostic defects with no write-path or security consequence (iteration 6, evidence: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`).\n215: - The five findings contradict each other -- ruled out: they name five separate surfaces (iteration 6, evidence: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`).\n216: \n217: ---\n218: \n219: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n220: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n221: - Dimension: none; the loop converges here. - Focus area: synthesis of the five P2 findings into the lineage report. - Reason: all four dimensions have coverage, the last two ratios are 0.40 and 0.00, and the composite vote clears 0.60. - Rotation status: complete. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: none. - Required evidence: the synthesis report, the closeout events and the release-readiness state. Review verdict: PASS\n222: \n223: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n224: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n225: \n226: - The pass-one report (`review/review-report-pass-1.md`) lists 43 merged findings; 17 belong to this area, all P2 after verification.\n227: - The remediation range is `320e7b64d4..HEAD` (HEAD `087888ec4a`); 21 doctor-install files changed.\n228: - The pass-one lineage (`review/lineages/doctor-install/`) stopped at its five-iteration cap with a last novelty ratio of 0.125, so this pass exists to verify the fixes and converge.\n229: - The doctor-install area touches four prompt-hook runtimes (claude, codex, cursor, devin); opencode, pi and dsh have no advisor hook entry in this checkout, and `hook-wiring-check.cjs` skips them by design.\n230: - Holdout files belong to the accuracy-runner area. This lineage opened none and reports counts only where a doc mentions them.\n231: \n232: ---\n233: \n234: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n235: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n236: [Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n237: \n238: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n239: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n240: | `spec_code` | core | pending | - | Packet docs read in iteration 4 |\n241: | `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | No checklist row claimed yet |\n242: | `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | - | No skill or agent definition in this area |\n243: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | Runtime coverage read in iteration 3 |\n244: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | Feature catalog describes the advisor, not the doctor routes |\n245: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | - | No playbook file in this area |\n246: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n247: \n248: ---\n249: \n250: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n251: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n252: [Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\n253: \n254: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n255: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n256: | [path/to/file] | [D1, D3] | [N] | [0 P0, 1 P1, 2 P2] | [partial/complete] |\n257: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n258: \n259: ---\n260: \n261: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n262: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n263: - Max iterations: 7\n264: - Convergence threshold: 0.10\n265: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n266: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n267: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n268: - Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-doctor-install-2-1794570021136-noekp0, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n269: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n270: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n271: - Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n272: - Severity threshold: P2\n273: - Review target type: spec-folder\n274: - Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n275: - Started: 2026-11-13T12:40:00.000Z\n276: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-install-2/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-276\n1: # Deep Review Strategy - Doctor Install Pass Two\n2: \n3: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n4: \n5: - Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder), area `doctor-install`.\n6: - Purpose: verify every pass-one doctor-install fix holds, review every file changed since pass one line by line, then look for new defects.\n7: - Mutability: updated by the orchestrator and by each iteration; reducer-owned counts are refreshed after every iteration.\n8: \n9: ---\n10: \n11: ## 2. TOPIC\n12: \n13: Review: command surfacing pass two, doctor-install lineage. Scope is the doctor install, setup, symlink, runtime-mirrors and AGENTS.md routes plus the scripts and tests they own.\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n18: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n19: [All dimensions complete]\n20: \n21: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n22: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n23: \n24: - Re-report a pass-one finding whose fix holds, a deferred item from report section 8, R4-P2-003, or the refuted finding.\n25: - Review any file outside the 30 doctor-install area paths.\n26: - Read or print holdout prompt text. The doctor-install area opens no holdout file.\n27: - Change code. This lineage writes only its own review packet.\n28: \n29: ---\n30: \n31: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n32: \n33: - Composite convergence score at or above 0.60 with all four dimensions covered, or seven iterations.\n34: - A P0 or P1 finding keeps the verdict at FAIL or CONDITIONAL; it never blocks recording the iteration.\n35: \n36: ---\n37: \n38: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n39: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n40: - [x] correctness\n41: - [x] security\n42: - [x] traceability\n43: - [x] maintainability\n44: \n45: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n46: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n47: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n48: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n49: - P1 (Required): 0\n50: - P2 (Suggestions): 5\n51: - Resolved: 0\n52: \n53: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n54: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n55: \n56: - Reading the remediation diff beside the pass-one one-line fix, then running the owning test file, kept every verdict tied to the bytes as they are now (iteration 1).\n57: - Running the check engine against this checkout and its test file beside the changed verdict branches proved the five check-engine fixes without a fixture-only claim (iteration 2).\n58: - Probing `hook-wiring-check.cjs` with temporary hook fixtures exposed wrapper shapes the unit tests do not cover (iteration 3).\n59: - Comparing the setup leg's hook-health claim against `metrics.ts` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` found a surviving pass-one doc defect (iteration 4).\n60: - Reading the remaining route manifest and the A10 JSON entries found two docs-versus-code gaps the changed rows did not cover (iteration 5).\n61: - Re-reading every cited finding line and the owning test files confirmed all five findings and no pass-one regression (iteration 6).\n62: \n63: ---\n64: \n65: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n66: \n67: - The new exit-3 contract covers `restored:` and `nothing was restored` but not the engine's `the restore failed` path, so the route has no branch for a partly written tree (iteration 1).\n68: - No check-engine fix failed in iteration 2. The one recorded limitation is the header assumption in `parseTableRows`, which every shipped router satisfies.\n69: - The narrowed hook-wiring matcher does not recognise `env node ...`, `node --no-warnings ...` or `bash -lc \"node ...\"` wrappers (iteration 3).\n70: - The pass-one Q3 repair names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` as the switch that turns hook-health records on; the writer records every prompt by default and the flag only adds two fields (iteration 4).\n71: - A10 still counts report-only INFO entries as \"copies as expected\", and the embed route names the backup folder `<timestamp>` where the engine uses the plan digest (iteration 5).\n72: - No new defect appeared in the final consistency pass; the remaining debt is the five P2 findings, not a failed fix.\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n77: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n78: ### **`setup.md` documents an out-of-repository write the workflow forbids** -- ruled out: the workflow invariant names the socket directory and the setup.md prose names the same directory (iteration 4, evidence: `doctor-setup.yaml:28`). -- BLOCKED (iteration 4, 1 attempts)\n79: - What was tried: **`setup.md` documents an out-of-repository write the workflow forbids** -- ruled out: the workflow invariant names the socket directory and the setup.md prose names the same directory (iteration 4, evidence: `doctor-setup.yaml:28`).\n80: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n81: - Do NOT retry: **`setup.md` documents an out-of-repository write the workflow forbids** -- ruled out: the workflow invariant names the socket directory and 